{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc","id":206054,"title":"(Recruitment Thread) Zodiac Beasts, OOC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-23T07:13:39-07:00","id":206054,"title":"(Recruitment Thread) Zodiac Beasts, OOC","content":"Actual RP Thread is located here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/205196-ic-zodiac-beasts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...-zodiac-beasts</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Zodiac Beast thread is designed for <b>up to</b> 13 people although we do not need to fill out the whole roster if that seems a bit too much for you guys. Not every slave manages to escape, after all. Anyways, these are the spots we currently have available.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Story Teller:</b> Taking the role of the Keeper, who's toying with the players for their own amusement. Players are pretty much dancing to his tune while simultaneously trying to find a way to escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Keeper - Thorbes (</b>I had to drop out)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Players:</b> Incarnations of the Chinese Zodiac, all of them Beast seeming. The beasts are somewhat Anthropomorphic, meaning they still have access to their humanoid appendages. That should come in handy when you're trying to pick a lock or solve a Fae puzzle!<br /> <br /> Due to the restrictive nature of everyone being members of the Beasts, and in order for them to not be mindless animals, I encourage players to be Dual Kith, preferably with the second Kith being from an alternate seeming.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rat - Open<br /> <br /> Dog - Open<br /> <br /> <b>Goat - Evilmarmelade</b><br /> <br /> Dragon - Open<br /> <br /> Rooster / Chicken - Open<br /> <br /> <b>Ox - Cire</b><br /> <br /> Rabbit - Open<br /> <br /> <b>Pig - Gaius</b><br /> <br /> Horse - Open<br /> <br /> Snake - Open<br /> <br /> Monkey - Open<br /> <br /> Tiger - Open<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The roles are first come, first serve. Whoever claims it gets the spot. Just list the following in your submission<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Role:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kith(s):</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Character Description:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Short Bio:</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T15:09:48-07:00","id":206597,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">If possible, I would like to play in this game. If it is open, I would take the Pig role, as that is my own Chinese Zodiac sign.<br /> <br /> Role: Oxen<br /> <br /> Kith: Beastling<br /> <br /> Year of Birth: 1985<br /> <br /> Character Description: Jessica Sparks is very short and slim with smooth features. She has short, brown hair, and dark brown eyes. She has a tattoo of a scarlet sports car on her left shoulder blade.<br /> <br /> Short Bio: Jessica Sparks is a locksmith from Mankato, Minnesota. She is annoyed by modern art (a passion of an ex), but a sucker for fast cars</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">. Jessica has a weakness for vanity, and strives for diligence. She also collects keys and figurines. She lives with her three cats and Curtis, boyfriend. Her favorite drink is brandy. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  To add year of birth 08-01-2014, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:15:42-07:00","id":206656,"title":"","content":"My Zodiac is the rabbit... a fire rabbit, apparently.<br /> <br /> As for Kith, I meant things like Hunterheart, Riddleseeker, and stuff like that. Beast is their seeming. I'm not sure if Kiths can be crossed between different seemings, but I think they can. Like a Swiftrunner + Gristlegrinder.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, thanks for signing up. I was afraid nobody was interested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:30:55-07:00","id":206724,"title":"","content":"I think kiths can be taken from different seemings. I will give some more thought to me. Perhaps it will become clear with time.<br /> <br /> As to interest, I would not be surprised if there are others who are interested, but lack the time due to other projects. It is for that reason I passed up several games that looked good, but I decided I just missed being player too much. I have just vowed to myself I won't let this game keep me from doing my level best for the one that I am running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T19:54:41-07:00","id":206742,"title":"","content":"Aww, seriously? The Pig had been the one I'd been eying and then BAM, first one gone. XD I admit that's disappointing, but I'm more amused than anything. Let's see if any of the other 10 start speaking to me...<br /> <br /> Kudos to you on trying to balance your various games, Cire. It's a tricky thing to manage, but very fulfilling.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Kiths, they generally serve as a &quot;specialization&quot; of sorts within the Seeming (so something playing up strengths of the animal side), but cross-Seeming Kiths are fine with ST approval. This could easily just be baked into this game's assumptions.<br /> <br /> One thought is also that some Changelings sort of &quot;grow into&quot; their Kiths over time, or develop them based on circumstance. It could make sense for some people to start without a Kith (or with only one), and then pick one/two/another up in play as appropriate.<br /> <br /> I've sometimes seen houserules that characters can start with the Dual Kith Merit for free, giving them two Kiths to pick out, typically one in-Seeming and one from wherever. It can lend more freedom toward concepts a player finds interesting.* I think that option could work well here: one Kith might reflect the particular animal's traits, while the other (if used) might go toward something else (maybe related to the sorts of tasks the Keeper sets, or further cruelties it inflicts, or whatever else).<br /> EDIT: Just saw you'd already mentioned the Dual Kith bit in the game description. Whoops! The rest still seems relevant.<br /> <br /> * I (regrettably only briefly) played a Nick Bottom-like fellow, using the Broadback and Minstrel Kiths (the latter refluffed as a Thespian). Can't remember if I went with Fairest or Beast with his Seeming...<br /> <br /> As one final point you'd raised in the game description, I don't think taking a non-Beast Kith is necessary. Strictly speaking, if we were going strictly by what the books say is typical, just having a Beast Seeming would have the mindless animal trait locked in for most of the Durance. The game's being flexible there in the name of an interesting story, so I don't think there's reason for a Kith limitation. If someone just wants to play up a character's animal side in the Kith(s), whether driven mostly by instinct or not, I think that should be fine.<br /> <br /> Hmm... No idea about a concept...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Missed the bit on Dual Kiths. 07-23-2014, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T19:58:50-07:00","id":206745,"title":"","content":"Gaius, I would be happy to switch from the Pig. I have no real attachment. As I said, I simply picked it because I was a pig. Please take it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T06:18:43-07:00","id":206977,"title":"","content":"Piggy gets lots of love, it seems. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, I may decide to take the role of Keeper after all. I may not know much about the game, but playing the villain has always been my specialty in free form RP's. And Changeling does give me the opportunity to really &quot;cut loose&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:46:27-07:00","id":207330,"title":"","content":"Great!<br /> <br /> With your permission, I'll switch to an Ox. Anything I can do to encourage another player is to the good in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T14:01:45-07:00","id":207517,"title":"","content":"Permission... GRANTED","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T14:44:33-07:00","id":207547,"title":"","content":"Thank you. Editing now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T15:02:03-07:00","id":207566,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm going to go ahead and claim the Keeper spot. I'll try to be as disturbing and twisted as the role demands. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:05:37-07:00","id":207762,"title":"","content":"Well I'm trying to keep this paced so if anyone else wants to join in, Cire's character won't leave them behind. Then again, maybe scattering them throughout this mad house would be even more fun. O_O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T19:04:05-07:00","id":207801,"title":"","content":"I also plan not to leave behind other players. Although maybe you are right about it being fun if they are scattered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T20:03:35-07:00","id":207849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=206745#post206745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaius, I would be happy to switch from the Pig. I have no real attachment. As I said, I simply picked it because I was a pig. Please take it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow. Wasn't expecting that. Was mainly just expressing my amusement. Still, thanks for the generosity! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd been mulling over taking the sheep (presuming I could sub in sheep for goat...?), but this works just fine, if you're sure.<br /> <br /> Ah, just to give our zodiacs: I'm a Fire Tiger. It crossed my mind to go with that. But I guess the more domestic animals just struck me as more interesting. Less common, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=206977#post206977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggy gets lots of love, it seems. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, who could say no to that face? ... Er, aside from the guy taking it in place of his own face against his will, I guess. ^_^o Though even then I imagine he doesn't so much &quot;say&quot; as &quot;scream.&quot; Eheh...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, I may decide to take the role of Keeper after all. I may not know much about the game, but playing the villain has always been my specialty in free form RP's. And Changeling does give me the opportunity to really &quot;cut loose&quot; </div> </div> </div>I approve of this notion. ^__^ You've posted up a storm in the C:tL forums and put a lot of interesting and creative things on display. It'll be interesting -- and for the characters, worrying -- to see what you do with a Keeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=207762#post207762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'm trying to keep this paced so if anyone else wants to join in, Cire's character won't leave them behind. Then again, maybe scattering them throughout this mad house would be even more fun. O_O</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see some fun either way, aye. I admit to liking for characters to get acquainted before circumstance splits them up singly or into groups (and brings them back together at its whims!). Again, I'm very open to sticking together or splitting up. Max will probably prefer to follow anyone strong and decisive around, though, like a lost piglet.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, not to hold up the second character's introduction any longer...<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Role:</b> Pig<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kith(s):</b> Unknown (Cleareyes, Rot-Eater, or Truefriend, maybe...?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Character Description:</b> Max Layton is slender and of average height for a nineteen year old. His dark brown hair is usually in need of a haircut and he keeps it pressed back, keeping it out of his green eyes. He isn't especially athletic, but has a bit of muscle tone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Short Bio:</b> Max is a college kid in San Antonio, Texas. Generally easy-going, he usually wears a friendly smile. He can be shy and overly sensitive, but the martial arts classes he's taken have done a lot for him the past few years. He's big on fantasy novels and games. He's not really sure what he wants to do with his life, and pretty okay with that, working a part-time job at a local bubble tea shop. He recently worked up the courage to ask out a childhood friend he's had a crush on. The little pig he picked up was meant to be a gift to her on their first date.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T21:08:52-07:00","id":207886,"title":"","content":"Max seems great. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T21:14:17-07:00","id":207890,"title":"","content":"Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm really liking Jessica, too. She definitely seems like she's got a better head on her shoulders than Max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T21:27:36-07:00","id":207896,"title":"","content":"Thank you. However, Jessica was luckily in her wheelhouse. That could so change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:34:36-07:00","id":207925,"title":"","content":"True enough. It's a big madhouse, and the Keeper's not even made an appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:57:00-07:00","id":208107,"title":"","content":"I've seen it called Sheep and Ram in the past, but when I googled the Zodiac, it said Goat, so either one works, really. Odd that I would be a Fire Rabbit, since my other Zodiac says &quot;Water - Sagittarius&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also excited to see how this RP goes. Most of the free form RP's I do on other websites are less so much about the plot as getting to the more &quot;adult&quot; content. It's good to focus more on a story for once, especially one with such interesting possibilities as Changeling. How can you go wrong with a setting that is specifically focused on madness and flipping off the laws of nature? Well okay, there are several ways it can go terribly, terribly wrong... <i>for the characters.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2015, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:19:42-07:00","id":208116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=207925#post207925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Keeper's not even made an appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wroooooong! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:46:31-07:00","id":208307,"title":"","content":"Aye, I don't think the western and eastern zodiacs are on the same elemental cycle. Which hey, works out all the better for diversity.<br /> <br /> Also, sorry to hear you've had bad luck with past sites charging full steam at, well, &quot;steamy situations.&quot; I've never been too big on that, myself, and aiming more for the plot and character side of things seems the norm around here. All to the good!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=208116#post208116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wroooooong! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, it was true for a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> 'sides, there's always trying to reason with him. Through his alien, idiosyncratic, and inconstant definition of &quot;reason,&quot; yes, but hey!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:49:55-07:00","id":208310,"title":"","content":"Oh it wasn't bad luck. That's kind of what the RP's were focused around. I'm just saying it's nice to take a break for once and focus on a more constructive story.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pfft, reason? That's for people bound by the laws of reality!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:57:23-07:00","id":208315,"title":"","content":"Ohh, now I gotcha. Thanks for clarifying. Also, sorry if it sounded like I was implying there was anything wrong with that kind of RP. It's not my preference, but as long as someone wasn't hoping for something else, everything's A-OK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:16:54-07:00","id":208350,"title":"","content":"<b>Keeper:</b> Mild punishment = hours of having pieces of your body carved off to feed hungry Changelings. You don't want to see Major punishment.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:20:29-07:00","id":208493,"title":"","content":"No, but I fear that we will before this is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:08:30-07:00","id":208799,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that bet's probably a safe one. I'm sure our pair of reluctant ungulates sure hope otherwise, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T17:00:40-07:00","id":208884,"title":"","content":"Hm. Maybe this is an odd line of thought, but... Are the player characters wearing clothes? I presumed they were wearing what they'd been taken in, though I could also see their Keeper wanting their bodies on full display or something. Or maybe attired in some traditional Chinese grab? If they had been naked, perhaps it was just the general stress (&quot;Clothing is the least of my problems right now!&quot;) or some subtle element of the beast on their ability to notice or care (&quot;What? No clothes? ... Hey, wow, you're right! Not... too bothered by it, though. Weird.&quot;).<br /> <br /> Regardless, odds are pretty good the recent visitors to the slaughterhouse are <i>now</i> less clothed than they would like to be. Though I guess any clothing might have magically left when they entered and returned when they left? &gt;.&gt; Eh, just trying to get a mental idea of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T21:37:21-07:00","id":209022,"title":"","content":"I would imagine they're wearing the shredded remains of their former clothing. Dragged through The Hedge while they slept and given new bodies, their human clothing would not have been able to withstand the punishment hostile environment and the new physiology. By now they probably resemble some kind of tribal savages, wearing scraps and rags.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, nobody likes eating dirty socks. Well some Fae probably would, they have weird lore like that. But I'd imagine meat is more appetizing than fabric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2015, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:17:23-07:00","id":209589,"title":"","content":"By the way, you both rock as writers. Just so you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T19:04:53-07:00","id":209696,"title":"","content":"D'aww, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't sell yourself short, though! You're doing great.<br /> <br /> Hm, also, random whimsical goofiness that's been bouncing around my head. Enjoy! Note: Enjoyment not compulsory.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">For Max:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">This little student went to market,<br /> This little student had plans.<br /> This little student chose poorly,<br /> This little Gentry thus said:<br /> &quot;And this little piggy went wee-wee-wee<br /> through the Thorns home.&quot;</div>For Jessica:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">There once was a maid who worked locks,<br /> Who found strange statuettes in a box.<br /> She gave correct pay,<br /> And that ended her day,<br /> The next thing she knows she's an ox.</div>And, hey, one for the sheep dude I'd considered:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Buyer starts to fall asleep,<br /> Quick as if he'd counted sheep.<br /> Fading fast he hears an elf:<br /> &quot;Don't forget to count yourself!&quot;</div>EDIT: 8/17/14<br /> For Nate:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A little lamb bought unadorned,<br /> Lulls singer in to sleep unthorned.<br /> Hours from the clock are torn,<br /> 'til the toll to which it's sworn.<br /> Now mother wakes to child unborn,<br /> And father wakes to spiraled horn.</div> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Added one for Nate. 08-17-2014, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T19:33:45-07:00","id":209713,"title":"","content":"That is great!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:25:58-07:00","id":209800,"title":"","content":"Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T22:14:26-07:00","id":209830,"title":"","content":"I did some math. If Max is 19 and was born in a year of the pig, it seems logical that our game is set in either 2002 or 2014. In either case, it would be the year of the horse. This might be obvious to everybody else, but I thought I would check to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T02:08:24-07:00","id":209968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=209589#post209589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, you both rock as writers. Just so you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>well I've been free form RPing for close to 10 years. Sadly, I don't have the same experience with table top RPing. One of the bad things about being born in the age of video games, I guess... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, thanks for pointing out the year, I had kind of lost track of it at some point. Last I heard, it was either Rat or Dog. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T12:59:41-07:00","id":210490,"title":"","content":"Ooh, thanks for doing the math, Cire. I realized I'd kind of dropped Max's age in carelessly, but it hadn't struck me that it could actually match up to 2014. Kinda neat! Though his age could easily be fudged a year or so in either direction. Anyway, if the the Pig is around 19 in 2014, then the Ox is probably around 29 in 2014. So... ^_^o Sorry for inadvertently inducing a general age in Jessica. Here's hoping that's near what you were aiming toward. We can probably still fiddle with things a bit.<br /> <br /> Also, Nyrufa raises a good point: practice makes perfect. I've been RPing and writing (kinda-sorta) for a long time. What skill I have, I attribute to that. And yeah, relative freeform RP definitely takes up a broader swath of my experience. :/ The friends I used to play tabletop RPGs with have regrettably gone to the winds some time ago, and I've had very poor luck with play-by-post for tabletop games (much as I keep trying). Still, you could always try looking up local tabletop groups and trying to find one.<br /> <br /> Also also, those bits of Zodiac verse of mine apparently got 3 likes, which, uh. o_o Wow. Thank you so much, you guys! ^__^<br /> <br /> But more importantly, that suggests we've got at least one reader! Hello, mysterious stranger! By all means, feel free to introduce yourself, drop in some regular color commentary, or let us know how you're liking things. ^_^ If you're of a mind to join in, there are still ten complimentary little statues to choose from. The recent change in scenery would be an especially natural opening for a new player, but anytime is fine. Of course, you're certainly welcome to keep browsing if you'd rather. Whatever you choose, here's hoping you're enjoying yourself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Wasn't digging that smiley. 07-27-2014, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:57:43-07:00","id":210553,"title":"","content":"That's correct, the Zodiac is still all in the same location as each other right now, so new players can still hop right in without too much trouble. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:27:14-07:00","id":210572,"title":"","content":"Hi! I'ts been a very entertaining and funny (say funny, say creepy...) reading so far. I can't beging to wonder how those poor things are going to escape the Collector and make their way back to the regular world.<br /> <br /> EDIT: loved the sheep rhyme by the way, it turns from childish to unsettling in just one line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 07-27-2014, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T21:49:57-07:00","id":212066,"title":"","content":"Glad you're enjoying it. I suspect the open ranch is probably going to have some part in the escape plan. Assuming having your body carved up for 3 hours didn't obliterate any notions of running away from home. They wouldn't want to make their master feel unloved, would they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:45:14-07:00","id":212199,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Thorbes. ^__^ I'm glad you're liking the thread and enjoyed the rhymes.<br /> <br /> It's definitely a tight spot they're in, but their chances certainly <i>appear</i> better of coming up with something, now that they're slightly more free to move about. But it was a pretty traumatic experience; they're no doubt cautious. It might help if they had a third head to put together, but we'll see if someone new takes an interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T03:37:46-07:00","id":212290,"title":"","content":"Maybe you can take advantage of the Horse? They is free, sort off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T20:06:54-07:00","id":214242,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I made a misstep. Great game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T05:23:47-07:00","id":214560,"title":"","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> I've never got to play Changelin, because it's really not popular where I come from (I'm french), so I don't really know a lot about the setting. Also, I've never tried freeform rp, but that sounds really interesting. I really like your setting, I'm a sucker for anything symbolic. So, can I join you? This could be a really cool way to work on my english skills. ^^<br /> <br /> By the way I'm a Metal Goat, and I'd gladly take this sign!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T05:30:06-07:00","id":214562,"title":"","content":"I, for one, think it would be great to have you in the game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T07:19:24-07:00","id":214631,"title":"","content":"@Thorbes: I'm kinda curious how things work with the &quot;animal of the year&quot; thing. Maybe just freedom to wander the Keeper's grounds, a year's leave to go home, or some other duty/activity? Time will tell! Though I'm sure none of the characters are eager to find out by it becoming their turn, given how long it will mean they've been there. Though Arcadia is known for lacking the most orderly sense of time.<br /> <br /> @Cire: No, no misstep that I can see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've just been busy and exhausted the last couple of days. I'm sorry I'm in too much of a rush this morning, too, but I'll try to post tonight.<br /> <br /> @Evilmarmelade: Cire is not for one: I'd be glad to see you in this, too! ^_^ It's also cool that you'll be using it to work on your English. Which is itself already impressive; I wouldn't have guessed you were a non-native English speaker if you hadn't said so. Anyway, yes! Looking forward to seeing your character for the Goat/Sheep, or whatever you wind up deciding!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T09:51:05-07:00","id":214754,"title":"","content":"Of course you can join! Freeform RPing is a great way to get your feet wet when it comes to role playing, or at least it's what got me hooked to it. I'm also in the same boat as you, I've bought two books (vampire and werewolf) but have nobody around here that plays it. D:<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, I find the books are great source material for writing stories. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T11:26:41-07:00","id":214883,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot guys!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=214631#post214631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also cool that you'll be using it to work on your English. Which is itself already impressive; I wouldn't have guessed you were a non-native English speaker if you hadn't said so. !</div> </div> </div> </div>And thank you again, it means a lot to me, as I'm currently working on my master's degree in english translation. ^^<br /> <br /> Anyway! <br /> <br /> <b>Role :</b> Ram<br /> <br /> <b>Kith</b> : Broadback<br /> <br /> <b>Character Description :</b> Nate Davis used to be a tall and slender man, with short blond hair. But that was before he met the Keeper. Now, he gained some muscles, along with goat legs covered in brown fur. His big ears are crowned with the curling horns of a ram, and he got a lot more hairy. His shaggy hair is now shoulder-length, and looks the same as the fur on his legs, coarse and brown. He's wearing a tattered and very loose-fitting Rolling Stones shirt<br /> <br /> <b>Short bio : </b>Nate, 23, was a golden boy. Born and raised in LA, he lived an easy life, his parents were kind but absent. He never had any money trouble, and was a spoiled brat. He used to take what he wanted, without any consequences. Nate is sarcastic and cynical, and can be seen as arrogant. Before being Taken, he was the lead guitarist in a small rock band called Wild Exhibit, who released two albums. He's kind of a jerk : he wasn't a stranger to cheating on women, and had just dumped his girlfriend Valerie because she told him she was pregnant. But he really doesn't care about that right now : he was the ninth person to be Taken, and has endured the Keeper's whims since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T11:34:30-07:00","id":214909,"title":"","content":"Approved for all audiences!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T18:09:33-07:00","id":215378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=214631#post214631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Cire: No, no misstep that I can see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've just been busy and exhausted the last couple of days. I'm sorry I'm in too much of a rush this morning, too, but I'll try to post tonight</div> </div> </div> </div>No rush on my end, and I totally understand! Just making sure I had not ruined a good thing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T22:11:55-07:00","id":215552,"title":"","content":"Nah, no worries, Cire. ^_^ All is well.<br /> <br /> Also, nice intro is nice. I admit I was wondering if one factor keeping people from signing up might be trouble justifying the relative silence from their character. This represents a good solution: interact vaguely with the other PC-less characters during &quot;timeskips,&quot; in turn giving anyone who picks them a character hook to use if they like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, wow! A master's degree in English Translation is really impressive. English always feels like it'd be a tricky one to get down, flagrant pickpocket of other languages that it is. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T22:24:54-07:00","id":215557,"title":"","content":"Gaius, I too am very impressed (and humbled) by Evilmarmelade's English. I also agree on the PC-less characters. I think Evilmarmelade has set a good example there as well.<br /> <br /> Evilmarmelade, thank you for joining!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:16:06-07:00","id":215666,"title":"","content":"Guys, stop it, you're making me blush. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I really don't think english is that difficult. French however, is a serious pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:24:18-07:00","id":215667,"title":"","content":"My dad taught me how to say &quot;What an ugly baby&quot; in French. I have no idea how to spell it, though, so I can't tell you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think I came up with a loop hole for the contract where they were taken prisoner. But like any good ST, I can't just give the answer away. I will say this though, might want to pay special attention to the wording on the contract. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-01-2014, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T03:06:47-07:00","id":215718,"title":"","content":"Oh, and don't hesitate to tell me if you can't understand my posts, or even if my wording isn't elegant. I could always do with some (positive!) criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:41:25-07:00","id":216213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=215667#post215667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My dad taught me how to say &quot;What an ugly baby&quot; in French. I have no idea how to spell it, though, so I can't tell you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>B\u00e9b\u00e9 laid? So says Google Translate, anyway! Which feels about right, if the adjective is correct and French puts its adjectives after the noun like Spanish and many others do (beb\u00e9 feo).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I think I came up with a loop hole for the contract where they were taken prisoner. But like any good ST, I can't just give the answer away. I will say this though, might want to pay special attention to the wording on the contract. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Well, always good to know a loophole exists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ... Though we could have probably guessed. The fey aren't big on any contract that's <i>ironclad</i>.<br /> *booed off-stage, pelted with overripe vegetables*<br /> <br /> Also, I know it looks like Matt's bit there at the end seems to be a response to your remark here, but I had actually been thinking about it a bit earlier. ^_^o Serendipity!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=215718#post215718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and don't hesitate to tell me if you can't understand my posts, or even if my wording isn't elegant. I could always do with some (positive!) criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can do. Doesn't seem like you'll need much of it, but we can pipe up if we spot something.<br /> <br /> Ah, actually, there is one small possible point I think I noticed in your first IC post. This is very nitpicky, but when Nate &quot;called them out,&quot; it might have been more appropriate to say, &quot;called out to them.&quot; The latter seemed to be the clear intent, given the context, that he was just getting their attention by calling in their direction. The former phrasing can mean that, but it's more often taken to mean one is challenging someone else (on a claim they've made, to a fight, about their scheme, on their hypocrisy, etc.). Again, it's still not wrong -- particularly if you were aware of this and meant it as Nate calling out Jessica and Max for engaging in a little plotting -- but I figured I'd mention it, just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  B\u00e9b\u00e9 laid y beb\u00e9 feo! 08-01-2014, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:52:38-07:00","id":216225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216213#post216213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> B\u00e9b\u00e9 laid? So says Google Translate, anyway! Which feels about right, if the adjective is correct and French puts its adjectives after the noun like Spanish and many others do (beb\u00e9 feo).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right, the proper wording would be &quot;Quel b\u00e9b\u00e9 laid&quot;, although you could easily replace laid by moche, hideux, affreux, monstrueux...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216213#post216213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can do. Doesn't seem like you'll need much of it, but we can pipe up if we spot something.<br /> <br /> Ah, actually, there is one small possible point I think I noticed in your first IC post. This is very nitpicky, but when Nate &quot;called them out,&quot; it might have been more appropriate to say, &quot;called out to them.&quot; The latter seemed to be the clear intent, given the context, that he was just getting their attention by calling in their direction. The former phrasing can mean that, but it's more often taken to mean one is challenging someone else (on a claim they've made, to a fight, about their scheme, on their hypocrisy, etc.). Again, it's still not wrong -- particularly if you were aware of this and meant it as Nate calling out Jessica and Max for engaging in a little plotting -- but I figured I'd mention it, just in case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right. I didn't pay attention to that. However, Nate clearly wants to scare them, so I may keep &quot;call them out.&quot;<br /> <br /> By the way, do we still need to eat and drink and defecate? If so, how are we fed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T16:17:35-07:00","id":216275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216225#post216225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right, the proper wording would be &quot;Quel b\u00e9b\u00e9 laid&quot;, although you could easily replace laid by moche, hideux, affreux, monstrueux...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I see. Thanks for the quick confirmation, correction and elaboration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, you're right. I didn't pay attention to that. However, Nate clearly wants to scare them, so I may keep &quot;call them out.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Aye, it began to seem more appropriate to me as I typed out that paragraph. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the way, do we still need to eat and drink and defecate? If so, how are we fed? </div> </div> </div>I'm entirely unsure. I admit to thinking they might not need to; Nyrufa hadn't mentioned anything about starving or getting fed while they were in the cages, so my brain kinda went off into the presumption that &quot;fey magic makes it unnecessary.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though, if so, that wouldn't mean the animal-cursed individuals might not think about eating or drinking anyway. I think Max has probably been freaked out by smelling buried mushrooms or acorns and briefly thinking they might make a good snack. Perhaps Jessica and Nate have had more thoughts of grazing than make them entirely happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T16:24:30-07:00","id":216280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216275#post216275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, if so, that wouldn't mean the animal-cursed individuals might not think about eating or drinking anyway. I think Max has probably been freaked out by smelling buried mushrooms or acorns and briefly thinking they might make a good snack. Perhaps Jessica and Nate have had more thoughts of grazing than make them entirely happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having to eat like an animal would be a good way to break someone' spirits, and I'm pretty sure the Keeper would love to see Nate and Jessica ruminate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T21:45:01-07:00","id":216417,"title":"","content":"That would be pretty funny, seeing them crawl around in the dirt, eating whatever they can find. But if the Slaughterhouse was any indication, they do need to eat. Hmm, maybe Jessica finds out she has four stomachs and needs to eat her food multiple times? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sure that would play havoc on her sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T22:38:38-07:00","id":216489,"title":"","content":"Good idea. I will try to work that in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T23:25:11-07:00","id":216536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216417#post216417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be pretty funny, seeing them crawl around in the dirt, eating whatever they can find. But if the Slaughterhouse was any indication, they do need to eat. Hmm, maybe Jessica finds out she has four stomachs and needs to eat her food multiple times? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm sure that would play havoc on her sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I dunno... It feels like something that'd be significant enough on their psyches to have gotten a mention before. Perhaps the Keeper -- possibly from an interaction with some of his many, many other Changelings -- had figured he'd let Celestial beings like the Chinese Zodiac go without needing to eat, but has recently changed his tune. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think a strict turn order is necessary, but could we maybe try to avoid having too much conversation between a couple of characters before others have had a chance to post? ^_^o I'm not the quickest of posters, and it's always been a pet peeve of mine to see a conversation fly by before I can contribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T23:45:27-07:00","id":216543,"title":"","content":"I know what you mean. I've had several forum based RP's fly upwards of 5 or 6 pages worth of posts before. I don't see that being a major problem here, since we've only got 4 players, but its still frustrating when it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T00:27:51-07:00","id":216557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216536#post216536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, I dunno... It feels like something that'd be significant enough on their psyches to have gotten a mention before. Perhaps the Keeper -- possibly from an interaction with some of his many, many other Changelings -- had figured he'd let Celestial beings like the Chinese Zodiac go without needing to eat, but has recently changed his tune. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they don't need to eat, and they just have very strong urges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T01:28:48-07:00","id":216601,"title":"","content":"Such was near my original thinking, and I'd certainly be on board with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T03:23:12-07:00","id":216633,"title":"","content":"So I've been wondering whether or not giving Ethan a dual kith, as he's also a musician. Adding Thusser or Ministrel seemed like a good idea.<br /> <br /> And then, while browsing the Changeling forum, I've found your thread about custom kiths, Nyrufa, and especially this ;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/178995-what-s-your-custom-kiths?p=183315#post183315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Satyr:</b> Hedonists with the legs and horns of a goat, but the arms, head, and torso of a human. Satyrs were kept prisoners in Arcadia by exploiting their lack of self control. Exquisite food, awesome music, potent liquor, and wild orgies were the shackles the Satyr had to break free of to make their way back to the mundane world. It is a misconception that all Satyrs are male, there are female Satyrs, but they're simply rarer in number. These Fairest often hope that the Free Holds can provide a more fulfilling life than the endless indulgence they came from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing - Party Animal: Satyrs learned how to have fun during their stay in Arcadia, and that knowledge remains with them after their escape. By spending a point of Glamour, the Satyr gains a +1 dice pool equal to their Wyrd Score on Crafts when it comes to Food, Drink, or Music. Additionally, they gain a +2 on Seduction rolls. This bonus lasts for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Nate didn't really have the chance to party since he was Taken, his behavior and looks may fit this description. Would it be okay with you if I slowly move him toward this kith? Or would you prefer him to be more animalistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T03:37:44-07:00","id":216636,"title":"","content":"I think I figured the loophole out, but I'll just wait and see. Or I can PM Nyrufa for confirmation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Nice touch with the other Zodiac, they will be far stranger that the chinese ones (I mean, Capricorn is half goat-half fish...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T04:25:11-07:00","id":216647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216543#post216543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you mean. I've had several forum based RP's fly upwards of 5 or 6 pages worth of posts before. I don't see that being a major problem here, since we've only got 4 players, but its still frustrating when it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, about that. You may have noticed that I have a different time schedule than all of you, due to me living in Europe (Right now, it's 1 pm here in France). I don't know where you come from, but you seem at your most active when I'm asleep. Now, it's not such a problem on weekends, but I'm starting a new job on Monday and I can't afford to stay up late. So I won't mind if you go on ahead, I don't want to slow you down. I'll try to catch up by posting daily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T05:52:33-07:00","id":216690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216633#post216633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been wondering whether or not giving Ethan a dual kith, as he's also a musician. Adding Thusser or Ministrel seemed like a good idea.<br /> <br /> And then, while browsing the Changeling forum, I've found your thread about custom kiths, Nyrufa, and especially this ;<br /> <br /> <br /> While Nate didn't really have the chance to party since he was Taken, his behavior and looks may fit this description. Would it be okay with you if I slowly move him toward this kith? Or would you prefer him to be more animalistic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind you using one of my custom Kiths at all. I was hoping somebody would use the ideas we came up with in there for future games. ^_^ May have to leave out the wild orgies part though, I'm still new to these forums and I don't know how &quot;adult&quot; the RP's are allowed to get here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And Thorbes, if you think you figured out the trick, go ahead and PM me, I want to see if anyone's got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T08:33:04-07:00","id":216761,"title":"","content":"Well we don't have to play those orgies, we could just allude to them. The way I see it, Nate's going to have lustful and wild urges, the ram's basic instincts getting stronger the more he stays in this realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:57:46-07:00","id":216831,"title":"","content":"Fade-to-black or references would probably be appropriate, true. Also, Thorbes guessed the answer. Everybody clap for him!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:25:14-07:00","id":216851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216831#post216831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fade-to-black or references would probably be appropriate, true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, that'd be my preference, too, and what I'm used to finding. I have no problem with a character going in that direction, just not a fan of depicting the actual, uh, &quot;activities.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Hm, with whom would Nate be having the orgies, anyway? All the characters available are PCs or PC-possible. I mean, I guess there could be tree-like nymphs or the Keeper could decide to &quot;give them some company&quot; with more animal-people or whathaveyou?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Thorbes guessed the answer. Everybody clap for him! </div> </div> </div>There we go! Put your hands (or hooves) together for Thorbes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a guess about the loophole, but I think I'll wait a little for Max to think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Matt =/= Max. ^_^o 08-02-2014, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:47:30-07:00","id":216896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=216851#post216851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Hm, with whom would Nate be having the orgies, anyway? All the characters available are PCs or PC-possible. I mean, I guess there could be tree-like nymphs or the Keeper could decide to &amp;quot;give them some company&amp;quot; with more animal-people or whathaveyou?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I was thinking. I won't force Nate's urges on you guys, don't worry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T14:08:21-07:00","id":216906,"title":"","content":"Oh, don't worry, I trusted you. xD I was just musing about the logistics involved.<br /> <br /> ... Also, just to clarify myself because I can see it otherwise given the context: when I said &quot;give them some company,&quot; I did <i>not</i> mean the Keeper just saying, &quot;Hey, here, have a sexually compatible bedroom* companion of your new species!&quot; so much as just, &quot;Here, have some more animal-/whatever-people,&quot; with whom interactions of any sort might take place. Which has potential interest, whether or not any such newcomers were people the zodiac characters knew from their human lives. This may have been obvious, but hey, clarity!<br /> <br /> * Note: Bedroom not included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-02-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T15:13:17-07:00","id":216986,"title":"","content":"Who's to say they don't already have companions? Plenty of things around them that could have once been people. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I doubt the Keeper would just make it rain lusty animals from the sky... or maybe he would, he's a True Fae...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:21:37-07:00","id":217094,"title":"","content":"You know, he's also enjoying foods and drinks, it's not all about orgies. X)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:14:45-07:00","id":217599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217094#post217094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, he's also enjoying foods and drinks, it's not all about orgies. X)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not with that attitude! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, I think we know it's general hedonism, not just the orgies. Just what satyrs are traditionally known for, I guess. Though maybe part of it is me: if Max gives in more to his wild/domesticated side, that'll be a <i>lot</i> of food and drink he'll be indulging in, too. So I guess points of contrast come quickly to mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:29:39-07:00","id":217605,"title":"","content":"I think that the difference between Max's and Nate's urges is the same difference than between a glutton and a gourmet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:39:54-07:00","id":217610,"title":"","content":"There's likely some truth to that. Goats are also reputed to eat pretty much anything, but aren't as well known for the quantities. That suggests Nate would be more discriminating. Meanwhile, one of Max's growing fears is that the Keeper might just drop off some sort of gilded trough full of slop that never empties, and trying to empty it would just be what he did for the rest of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T16:02:59-07:00","id":217627,"title":"","content":"Well, Max will beat almost anybody else to a punch in a orgy, did you know pigs have orgasms in the half-hour mark? It has its perks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T18:12:59-07:00","id":217706,"title":"","content":"You're the second one to tell me that, I wasn't sure if it was true the first time, but now I'm reconsidering.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the point of the Satyrs (in the manner I wrote them up) is that their durance wasn't traumatizing, so much as paradise. They're a form of Fairest, rather than Beast. They had to make an active choice to leave behind the pleasures they were subjected to, not many people have that kind of willpower.<br /> <br /> Paradise was just as much a prison to them as any hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-03-2014, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:35:05-07:00","id":217844,"title":"","content":"I'm really enjoying this game. I very much hope that it is open-ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:42:29-07:00","id":217846,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I usually just make this stuff up as I go along. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:12:48-07:00","id":217861,"title":"","content":"I noticed we don't have many active RP's here. I wanted to do a vampire RP (maybe even one that takes place in the medieval ages) but can't come up with a decent plot. Also, I don't know very much about geography or history and would probably just butcher everything.<br /> <br /> D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:35:34-07:00","id":217875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217627#post217627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Max will beat almost anybody else to a punch in a orgy, did you know pigs have orgasms in the half-hour mark? It has its perks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a contest you guys! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217706#post217706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the point of the Satyrs (in the manner I wrote them up) is that their durance wasn't traumatizing, so much as paradise. They're a form of Fairest, rather than Beast. They had to make an active choice to leave behind the pleasures they were subjected to, not many people have that kind of willpower.<br /> <br /> Paradise was just as much a prison to them as any hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be one of the Keeper's games. If Nate's a bad goat, his tortures will remind him of his animal state. If he behaves, he could be rewarded by having seemingly &quot;human&quot; pleasures, like food and drinks and such, but in truth it's just a way to appeal to the domesticated farm animal in him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217844#post217844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really enjoying this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too! To be honest I've set up my alarm clock half-an-hour earlier that I'm supposed to, just so I could read you and respond before going to work. ^^ <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I want to apologize to Jessica on behalf of Nate. He is a misogynistic jerk after all, who may need a good slap or two. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-04-2014, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T07:35:02-07:00","id":218135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217627#post217627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Max will beat almost anybody else to a punch in a orgy, did you know pigs have orgasms in the half-hour mark? It has its perks.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217875#post217875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a contest you guys! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think I've heard of an orgy with a Win Condition before. xD Or maybe they do, I'm not the best informed. I just imagine most who go to orgies see <i>the orgies themselves</i> as the Win Condition.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I've heard that fun fact before. If it holds for him, I wonder how Max would feel about that. Well, possibly aside from, &quot;Yeah, woulda been nice to have sex as a full-human <i>once</i>...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=217844#post217844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really enjoying this game. I very much hope that it is open-ended.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]Me too! To be honest I've set up my alarm clock half-an-hour earlier that I'm supposed to, just so I could read you and respond before going to work. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, I'm having a lot of fun with this, as well. ^_^ Really looking forward to seeing where it goes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could be one of the Keeper's games. If Nate's a bad goat, his tortures will remind him of his animal state. If he behaves, he could be rewarded by having seemingly &quot;human&quot; pleasures, like food and drinks and such, but in truth it's just a way to appeal to the domesticated farm animal in him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that's a cool, insidious idea. Bit of a Xanatos Gambit. The carrot and the stick both lead to the same place.<br /> <br /> Hm, I'm wondering what sort of overall conflict Max might have... Right now, he wants to be strong, but he's too easily torn between wallowing in self-pity and, er, wallowing in the mud and other swinish indulgences to drown out the situation. I dunno. Feels like it might be a bit too depressing to linger on it overlong, and could use some other element to spice up this porkchop. I wonder how the Keeper might get more personally involved in his development...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:07:33-07:00","id":218235,"title":"","content":"I imagine the piggy's going to have the o_0 expression on his face the first time he discovers this little 'perk'<br /> <br /> <br /> Now how to go about this? So many limitless possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}