y reading your posts, you write with a really intricate style. Everyday I get up half an hour earlier so I can read your morning post (well, it's morning for me at least!) and try to answer it. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T04:06:01-07:00","id":227739,"title":"","content":"Quite the hefty post on your part. ^_^<br /> <br /> Something I forgot to mention earlier, by the way. I didn't mean to imply both Max and Nate joined in the orgy, my thoughts on the subject where that Nate screwed until he dropped, and Max was gorged on drugged shrooms. Sorry if it seemed like I forced Max to act against his character. Also, let's not forget we have Cire waiting to stumble upon this den of depravity. Unless they're getting a good show out of this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T05:40:14-07:00","id":227805,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we should probably end the flashback soon, unless Max has something else to do. Nate is going to, as Nyrufa said, screw until he drops, and unless he decides to fight Max for the attention of the nymphs *, he doesn't have much more to do (Not that ravishing six women isn't an exhausting work!).<br /> <br /> *And we could even do this while Jessica's here, watching two baked guys fighting while being attacked by crazy amphibian elves!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T07:07:21-07:00","id":227902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=227607#post227607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaaawww, Max' such a Truefriend!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be how it's working out, aye. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, I don't mind you being slow. I really enjoy reading your posts, you write with a really intricate style. Everyday I get up half an hour earlier so I can read your morning post (well, it's morning for me at least!) and try to answer it. ^^ </div> </div> </div>Aww, thanks. ^_^ I enjoy reading your posts, too, (and Cire's and Nyrufa's, for that matter), so it's a treat to read them after waking up for me, too. Not as long as mine, but that's irrelevant; brevity, soul, wit, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=227739#post227739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite the hefty post on your part. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I do sometimes get carried away. ^_^o<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something I forgot to mention earlier, by the way. I didn't mean to imply both Max and Nate joined in the orgy, my thoughts on the subject where that Nate screwed until he dropped, and Max was gorged on drugged shrooms. Sorry if it seemed like I forced Max to act against his character. </div> </div> </div>Aye, thanks, but no apology needed. I later figured that was the way of it, just wasn't my initial reading. Like I said, I was concerned I may have sent the wrong message on the direction Max was headed; had my initial reading been correct, I couldn't have blamed you for getting that impression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, let's not forget we have Cire waiting to stumble upon this den of depravity. Unless they're getting a good show out of this? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=227805#post227805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we should probably end the flashback soon, unless Max has something else to do. Nate is going to, as Nyrufa said, screw until he drops, and unless he decides to fight Max for the attention of the nymphs *, he doesn't have much more to do (Not that ravishing six women isn't an exhausting work!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'd be on board with ending it here, or maybe with one more post if Evilmarmelade has an idea; I can't think of anything significantly different Max will be getting up to, unless something acts on him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *And we could even do this while Jessica's here, watching two baked guys fighting while being attacked by crazy amphibian elves! </div> </div> </div>Only in Changeling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ... Note to self: moderate use of quotations to avoid posts ballooning in size. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T07:55:21-07:00","id":227940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=227902#post227902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I'd be on board with ending it here, or maybe with one more post if Evilmarmelade has an idea; I can't think of anything significantly different Max will be getting up to, unless something acts on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, I won't be able to post until late tonight, and it's 5 p.m. for me right now, so, if you want to carry on, please proceed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am seriously exhausted tonight and I can't hold my eyes open. I'm sorry, I' going to bed early.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-14-2014, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T01:48:01-07:00","id":228896,"title":"","content":"(ooh, how I like to double post)<br /> Nyrufa, I have a question. Do you plan on ending our game after we escape from Arcadia, or will we continue to play our new Changeling lives?<br /> <br /> I'm fine with both. I was just wondering if we'll have to involve ourselves with the Courts and all that. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:11:05-07:00","id":229261,"title":"","content":"Hmm, might make a continuation RP after the escape. I should warn that I've never actually owned the rule book, which is one major reason I set it in Arcadia, where anything is possible. I think I've got a rough interpretation of its performance, though. At least enough to run a free-form version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:46:02-07:00","id":229698,"title":"","content":"If you're not feeling inspired we could always do a &quot;where-are-they-now&quot; epilogue. In fact, this would be the first time that one of my campaigns ends officially.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-16-2014, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:07:24-07:00","id":229886,"title":"","content":"Aye, I could see it going either way. Might be interesting to have a completed story, but hey! ^_^ We can cross that bridge when we come to it.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not completely sure about my latest post. I <i>definitely</i> took some liberties with it. I'm certain it's not going to stick, and may never come up again, but I thought it might be interesting for the moment. I am A-OK rewriting it with Max as his typical pink and cuddly self.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Hunh. Don't usually forget half of what I wrote mere minutes after writing it. XD So, looks like I left some wiggle room in there: it could be that Max <i>actually</i> changed, it could be that Max will be <i>perceived</i> to have changed, or it could just be that Max <i>feels</i> like he changed.<br /> <br /> Also, Cire, I basically had it that Max saw Jessica's Mask, or what she looked like before. If you have any objections on that front, just lemme know! He may not even remember details when he comes back to his senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Blathering! 08-15-2014, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:44:31-07:00","id":229904,"title":"","content":"No objections at all, Gaius. As to going forward after the Durance, I personally hope that we do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T22:01:28-07:00","id":229957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=229698#post229698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're not feeling inspired we could always do a &quot;where-are-they-now&quot; epilogue. In fact, this would be the first time that one of campaigns ends officially.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I'm not inspired (indeed, I find Changeling one of the most interesting games), it's just that I'd pretty much be tossing a random assortment of ideas I've grabbed off the internet together, rather than having a more in depth understanding. But then again, this is free form, so maybe we could pull it off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think turning Max into a Boar mid combat is a problem. Indeed, I like how you guys are changing Kiths randomly depending on the situation. This is an origin story, after all, so it makes perfect sense that they'd still be adjusting to their roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2014, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T02:31:58-07:00","id":230084,"title":"","content":"Changing Max was definitely an interesting twist!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've been browsing thourgh the wikipedia article on sheep, and I found this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Despite these perceptions, a </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Illinois_system\" target=\"_blank\">University of Illinois</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monograph\" target=\"_blank\">monograph</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> on sheep reported them to be just below pigs and on par with cattle in </span></span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligence_quotient\" target=\"_blank\">IQ</a>. </div> </div> </div>T_T","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-16-2014, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:31:42-07:00","id":230561,"title":"","content":"Ah, I'm glad things seem well-received on that last post. ^_^ Always concerned about overstepping boundaries.<br /> <br /> @Cire: Thanks, I'm glad it's not an issue. And aye, like I said, I could be happy either way. I'm enjoying these characters and would like to follow them, but it would also be the first time I've started a game with an intent to tell one story, told that one story, and stopped, and there's an interesting feeling, there. Really, it's a matter of 'I won't be disappointed,' whatever happens.<br /> <br /> @Nyrufa: We could always frame it less as sticking strictly to Changeling: The Lost and more as something very heavily inspired by and drawing from that game. That seems like it might lay to rest some of your trepidations. It could also keep those of us better acquainted with C:tL as written on our toes, as we may not know what to expect.<br /> <br /> Aye, definitely makes sense that things would be less solidly rooted from the get-go. I've also kinda gotten the impression from reading online Changeling character origin stories that it's pretty common for a character to have... properties in Arcadia that they very definitely don't in-play, which are either explained away or just sort of fade during/after the escape (e.g. a woman turned into a dragon several stories tall ultimately finds a thin crack in her den, and wears and scratches her massive body away into something relatively human-sized in the effort of getting through). It makes sense that the characters would have the potential to explore a full assortment of relevant Kiths. If we go for the &quot;drawing inspiration from&quot; option, settling on a Kith may not be something that needs to happen; the Arcadia-granted properties can come up when they're relevant and fade when they aren't.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I don't anticipate the Boar sticking around for more than the next post or two, nor of Max getting a Bruce Banner deal going on. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> We'll see, though.<br /> <br /> @Evilmarmelade: Aww, cheer up. ^_^ Pigs are known to be very intelligent, and I've seen goats and sheep appear on some lists of smart animals, too, so I don't think there's a vast gulf. It's also worth considering that measuring animal intelligence is kinda tricky, and without a universal standard. I mean, with all the different physiologies, there probably <i>can't be</i> a universal standard. And that's before considering that the notion of IQ itself is controversial. There are many different types of intelligence and a given test is by its nature going to have to prioritize some over others, not least because some types of intelligence can be very hard to measure in quantitative terms.<br /> <br /> So, really, that bit just says that sheep and cattle are on about the same level just below pigs based on whatever standards of intelligence a particular test selected. There could be ways in which sheep and cattle think circles around the porkers and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> ... So, yes, I'm not <i>just</i> long-winded in my IC posts. ^_^o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:47:23-07:00","id":230573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=230561#post230561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I don't anticipate the Boar sticking around for more than the next post or two, nor of Max getting a Bruce Banner deal going on.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://imgflip.com/i/b7xf4\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/b7xf4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T14:53:00-07:00","id":230575,"title":"","content":"You're surprised that an animal which eats everything around it (including metal and garbage) has low intelligence? Anyways, I've been told several times that the games don't have to be played by the rails set out by the books. Perhaps even less so since we're doing free form without all the complicated attributes and dice rolls. They said the books could be a good starting point, but encouraged me to come up with my own settings too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I've watched enough reviews, read the wikis, and even seen some online sessions that I know the gist of how the game works. The Courts, the Goblin Markets, the Fruits, Hedge, Contracts, all the basics needed for good story telling. The major thing I'm in the dark about is the game play mechanics featuring dice rolls and such. Other than that, I know about the setting and background.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, features come and go, like an Elemental being turned into a mountain or a piece of the sky. Granted <b>The Incredible Pig</b> would be rather amusing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:16:49-07:00","id":230608,"title":"","content":"Playing this game with you actually made me pick up the book, and I now want to run a game irl for my friends in France, so they can discover the awesomeness that is The Lost. We got The Dreaming, but we didn't get many games in the New World of Darkness, only Vampire and Werewolf. Of course, I'll have to translate a lot of rules on character creation, since I'm the only one who's fluent enough in english, and I can't do a rule-free game with my usual tables : I don't think they'd like a game that focuses mainly on their character's psychology, and I'm too nice of a GM* when I don't have rules to rely on. Anyway, I think I'm gonna include Max, Jessica and the Keeper as NPC to my campaign, if that's all right with you all!<br /> <br /> *I've been GMing since I was 16, and I've only killed one PC since, and it was during the final fight of a short campaign, with an epic sacrifice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:33:54-07:00","id":230619,"title":"","content":"How could I be anything but honored?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:42:40-07:00","id":230622,"title":"","content":"That sounds awesome! Personally, the idea that it relates to the player's psychology is what's so alluring about the game. It asks the player to look inside themselves and think about how their character would actually react to various situations. Too many games are hack and slash mentality, whipping out powers at every obstacle. I love the mature setting for the World of Darkness, and how it takes a more realistic view on the supernatural concept. We need more games like that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:50:23-07:00","id":230627,"title":"","content":"I also think it's awesome, but unfortunately I don't know that many players interested by a &quot;serious&quot; game like this one. I already have enough trouble convincing my players to write a complete backstory...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T16:05:23-07:00","id":230650,"title":"","content":"Well granted, writing a full in depth background is kind of a chore for new players. I've been RPing since I was 15, and got better over time with experience and practice. I'd recommend starting them off with something basic, and as they get more interested in playing, then branch out to more complicated stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T16:22:08-07:00","id":230680,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I've thought about sending them small questions just to flesh out their characters, like &quot;what do you think of the different courts, what is your favourite food, what does your room look like, where do you hang out for fun&quot;, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:42:31-07:00","id":231006,"title":"","content":"Aye, I'm with Cire. ^_^ I'd be thrilled if you wanted to include Max and the other characters. Also very cool that this inspired you to try for a game among your friends. Let us know how it goes!<br /> <br /> I don't think there's anything wrong with some players being less interested in exploring the psychological aspects. It's unfortunate if they're disinclined to take advantage of that part of what Changeling offers, since it does offer so much in that area. But different people have different preferences, and I think Changeling can support a lot of them. So long as everyone's on the same page about what's happening, that should still make for an enjoyable game.<br /> <br /> And even if they're going in for one part or certain parts of it -- for instance, the game allows a <i>ridiculous</i> diversity in character concepts -- they'll still be adjacent to other aspects they may not have really considered or encountered before, or hadn't seen in the same light. It's probably best not to force these things -- people's preferences don't change easily -- but it's always a possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:41:33-07:00","id":231925,"title":"","content":"Double-posting, but eh. I apparently missed a couple of things on the last page, somehow.<br /> <br /> @Evilmarmelade: That is quite a pic. XD I'm sure Max would find it flattering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=230575#post230575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're surprised that an animal which eats everything around it (including metal and garbage) has low intelligence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the context of that line was that people often think they're dumb, when they actually aren't. I mean, by the standards of non-human animals, pigs are also really smart, and if the &quot;eats everything around it&quot; argument is true of goats, it's <i>definitely</i> true of pigs. I recall reading someone's account of how they were in Hawaii, and saw an empty plastic garbage can that a boar had apparently taken a huge bite out of, despite there being an abundance of much more palatable things to eat around it. I think the message is not, &quot;They're dumb,&quot; so much as, &quot;They can take it and cannot be bothered to give a damn.&quot;<br /> <br /> The rant of which it was part was actually pretty entertaining. &gt;.&gt; I'mma see if I can track it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:12:23-07:00","id":231944,"title":"","content":"I hope Nate's profanities in the last post are not a problem. I really think he's the type of guy who swear when he's angry, and...well...he kinda is, right now.<br /> In fact, I picture him exactly like this :<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pZZkqqc5uXM\" data-code=\"pZZkqqc5uXM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pZZkqqc5uXM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-17-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:30:04-07:00","id":231958,"title":"","content":"Nah, it doesn't bother me, and it fits really well. I was on the fence of whether Max would catch sight of Nate or just break down crying and do something similar at the whole affair. Nice job, by the way; really visceral scene, there. ^_^ Poor Nate...<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know if I got the exact feel I was going for, but I kinda like this. Lemme know, or I could always try something else.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A little lamb bought unadorned,<br /> Lulls singer in to sleep unthorned.<br /> <br /> Hours from the clock are torn,<br /> 'til the toll to which it's sworn.<br /> <br /> Now mother wakes to child unborn,<br /> And father wakes to spiraled horn.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":"also lambs are gentler than rams which i guess matters 08-17-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:34:33-07:00","id":231964,"title":"","content":"Ooooh, that's wonderfully creepy, I like it! Thanks man!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:40:39-07:00","id":231967,"title":"","content":"Ahh, great. ^__^ Glad to hear you like it! I'll add it to the first three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:21:29-07:00","id":232013,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Jessica's experiment will work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:03:58-07:00","id":232050,"title":"","content":"Might well do so. Let's see how things proceed; I could see Nate not being in the mood, though.<br /> <br /> Also, missed the video: I'd completely forgotten that movie, but the scene's a great fit. Right down to both being about how one's eyes work/look.<br /> <br /> ... I also kinda felt like doing something similar when Firefox exploded halfway through my post. &gt;_&lt; *sigh* Never gets any less unpleasant, and my 'periodically copy to Notepad' tactic always seems to be forgotten <i>right</i> when it rasslfrasselarghable...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:23:02-07:00","id":232067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=232013#post232013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Jessica's experiment will work!</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution was figured out a while ago by one of our audience. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Hope they're still reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:45:41-07:00","id":232081,"title":"","content":"I've still got my own guess on a loophole, but I'd hazard Cire meant the current idea of trying to make a pledge.<br /> <br /> But aye, I hope you're still reading, Thorbes. ^_^ If there's any chance anyone else is looking on, by all means give a hello, even if you don't feel keen on joining in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:39:34-07:00","id":232403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=232050#post232050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, missed the video: I'd completely forgotten that movie, but the scene's a great fit. Right down to both being about how one's eyes work/look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! I absolutely didn't make the connection, but this is rather fitting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:00:45-07:00","id":232698,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading. I was thinking on stoping because of a... let's say trigger-ish scene, but eventually kept following the story.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of joining as the monkey aand suggest or hint the solution IC, but thought it could be too Deus Ex Machina. Is way easier than you may think. Those are the complicated ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:21:13-07:00","id":232708,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about the scene with Nate and the green nymphs? If so, I'm sorry it made you uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see you join, actually. Even if it isn't for giving us the solution. In fact, I too have an idea of the correct answer to the riddle, but Nate isn't really in the mood for this right now. X)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T05:43:08-07:00","id":232727,"title":"","content":"It's the one in wich the goat basically jumps on some of the fish women with the intent of &quot;breding them&quot; even by force, actually.<br /> <br /> I'll think about it. I was pointed in the direction of this game before it started by Cire as we were buddies in a series of pbp Mage games in the old forums, but I was a bit down due to the most recent one dying with a whimper and wasn't ready to make the comminment to a regular game at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:04:35-07:00","id":232830,"title":"","content":"Oh, Thorbes, I put in an &quot;Easter Egg&quot; in for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:19:25-07:00","id":232842,"title":"","content":"Aye, sorry you were made uncomfortable, but I'm glad it didn't stop you from reading. :/<br /> <br /> And I definitely understand about having post-game blues like that. I've had so many PbP experiences die on me over the years, and it's always a real letdown for me, too. If you decide to, we'd be glad to have you in on this, be it as the Monkey or whichever else strikes your fancy. ^_^ If not, still glad to have you as a reader.<br /> <br /> The idea I've had in mind is also more simple than the ones Jessica has considered. Heh, I actually thought of a couple of other plausible loopholes when I woke up this morning. We'll see how we all handle things!<br /> <br /> Also, Thorbes, I meant to say so earlier -- and probably the first time I glanced you around sometime -- but you have one of the coolest signatures I've ever seen. ^__^<br /> <br /> Ah! And throwing out one last bit of thinking, if we're considering having the game go beyond the Durance, it would probably work best for everyone to have been taken from the same town. Maybe Jessica's, for simplicity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:27:46-07:00","id":232848,"title":"","content":"Well, the way I see it is that our heroes could emerge from the hedge anywhere in the world. We could pick a location together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:53:02-07:00","id":232862,"title":"","content":"If you'd like to join in, you're certainly welcome to do so, Thorbes. Perhaps the monkey would be a useful addition to the group, namely the ape-strength, and not being something others consider as food. Besides, this seems like the only RP that's still active. Unless I haven't been paying attention to the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you're all taken from the same town, that could make sense, you all stopping in at the same shop. Then again, the Keeper could just move their shop around the world after each purchase. ^_^ But yeah, everybody being from the same town could suit better for loose end scenarios of them trying to figure out what's become of their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Okay yeah, I wasn't paying attention, others are still alive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-18-2014, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:04:23-07:00","id":232877,"title":"","content":"My Mage game still lives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:56:51-07:00","id":232941,"title":"","content":"We already established that we weren't from the same town. However, we could indeed emerge in the same city.<br /> <br /> I'd like to address the matter of Nate's kid though. But that doesn't mean we all have to go to LA, I could do it on my own.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Thorbes. Again, I'm sorry it made you uneasy. However, I can guarantee that it wasn't without any consequences. Nate doesn't quite realize yet what he just did.<br /> <br /> Edit : I'd just like to thank all of you again for this game. I'm having a hard time this month and I'm not in a really good place, but this game keeps me busy in an awesome way, and that's all I need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-18-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:59:32-07:00","id":233165,"title":"","content":"RE: towns of origin<br /> Aye, I know it's been established that they're from all over the States before. It was mainly floating the idea of retconning them all to one spot for the basic reason Nyrufa said. Exploring elements of the lives from which they were taken is something I know we're all interested in seeing. It's easier to do if they're all in one spot with all they used to know.<br /> <br /> Though of course that's far from the only way to explore things. Some distance could add something, and &quot;commuting&quot; via the Hedge is an option, albeit one that's never completely safe. Another thought could be each of them emerging at a different time (and place), and then ultimately converging somewhere and somewhen, possibly handled by way of timeskip or an accelerated understanding of time, with flashbacks for important stuff that's passed up. I'm open to whatever we do, just so long as the characters have a chance to see and react to whatever may have happened in their absences.<br /> <br /> @Nyrufa: Definite boons to be had in none of the characters looking at each other as food. They clearly don't need help creating drama for themselves, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Monkey would also be a flexible sign, and give some contrast to the present group's Old McDonald Singalong. Raw ape strength as you've suggested is a fine option, though my first guess was a greater focus on the nimble, dextrous, flexible traits; the present team could do with some of that.<br /> <br /> @Evilmarmelade: Aww, I'm sorry to hear things haven't been going so hot for you lately. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, I'm glad we've helped, even if just a little. Here's hoping things take a turn for the better, and soon. If you think it might help to vent sometime, just pipe up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:31:05-07:00","id":233190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I definitely understand about having post-game blues like that. I've had so many PbP experiences die on me over the years, and it's always a real letdown for me, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know this things happen, but I felt responsible for this particular one dying out and felt like I let down my Mage buddies from the previous 2-3 games. I felt so ashamed I avoided posting in the same threads as MysticJackal (the one runing the game) because I couldn't bear the guilt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]you have one of the coolest signatures I've ever seen. ^__^</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I can't remeber from were I took it, but I cannot take credit for it. Pretty neat, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'd like to join in, you're certainly welcome to do so, Thorbes. Perhaps the monkey would be a useful addition to the group, namely the ape-strength, and not being something others consider as food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. And note that it's the closest to a human, that probably make dealing with the change somehow easier. Also Sun-Wukong!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Thorbes. Again, I'm sorry it made you uneasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I'm perhaps more sensitive of that issue than I have the right to be. Anyway, I didn't think worse of you for that. This is a game and I understood that the way the character and the player are can and do differ a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Thorbes, I put in an &quot;Easter Egg&quot; in for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is... this prehaps?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessica</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Years ago, I took a history class once, and I remember the professor - <b>Doctor Webster</b> - talking about.....&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Cire's (the Mage character, in case anyone is wondering <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) Real Name, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:55:38-07:00","id":233300,"title":"","content":"Great, now I'm imagining Thorbes jumping around, laughing while he bashes Fae brains in with a magic stick!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:14:41-07:00","id":233326,"title":"","content":"@Thorbes: Ahh... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hear you. I'm usually not the one who drops the ball, but there was an occasion with an amazing Exalted ST and I've always felt guilty about kinda... falling out of it.<br /> <br /> And heh. ^_^ There's some charm to the Monkey King notion. I'd be pleased with that direction, if Thorbes settles on it.<br /> <br /> Though if the Keeper decided to put on a show, I'm unsure how Max would respond to being handed a rake and drafted into a retelling of Journey to the West, starring Thorbes's character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Rearrangement and addition! 08-18-2014, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:32:29-07:00","id":233337,"title":"","content":"Good catch,Thorbes. <img 