 kind of impressive! If it doesn't, well... Heh, barring deus ex machina, Max was fun while he lasted. ^_^o<br /> <br /> Don't think I've taken a gamble like this with a character before, so let's see how it plays. Provided the Keeper's not scared of the little piglet, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> * EDIT: Also also, still more apologies, as I kinda felt the post was a little meh and... for lack of a better word, &quot;ham-handed&quot; toward the end. Need moar practice...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 02-03-2015, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T23:08:01-08:00","id":391077,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I can't wait to see what happens next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T02:45:59-08:00","id":391181,"title":"","content":"So, Gaius, exactly what you are asking the keeper?<br /> <br /> 1)You want to re-write the terms of the original Contract and make them retroactive.<br /> <br /> 2)You also want that anyone under the original Contracts can switch to this new one if they want.<br /> <br /> 3)Finally, as part of the new retroactive Contract you, personally not neccesarily the others, agree to explicitely become owned heart and soul by the Keeper.<br /> <br /> Are those terms correct? I want to be sure before proceeding.<br /> <br /> And regarding that little piece of trivia: yes, Cire and I, we go years back when we played together in some Mage Epistolary Chronicles in the previous iteration of these Fora and so when they notice this game asked me if I would like to join in. At the time I was still very sad for the last game that died out (for what I feel responsible) so wasn't too keen on doing it again, but... well, you know how that turned out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-03-2015, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T03:46:24-08:00","id":391215,"title":"","content":"Aaaaw, I just want to give Max a hug right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T03:55:39-08:00","id":391223,"title":"","content":"Right? He is such a sweet piece of pork <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mmmmm, we'll see how things turn out. I think I figured out ways to twist the demands of all of you. Remeber though that the Keeper is just giving you <i>the chance</i> to get what you are asking for, is not &quot;ask and you'll be given&quot;, that'd been boring.<br /> <br /> Anyway the chronicle is aproaching its end. Hope it is a satisfactory end at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:43:38-08:00","id":391253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391223#post391223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remeber though that the Keeper is just giving you <i>the chance</i> to get what you are asking for, is not &quot;ask and you'll be given&quot;, that'd been boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why Nate asked bluntly for home. I didn't have any idea on what he could ask for, i decided to go for the obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:48:51-08:00","id":391256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391253#post391253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's why Nate asked bluntly for home. I didn't have any idea on what he could ask for, i decided to go for the obvious.</div> </div> </div> </div>You suuuuuureeeeee?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nate the Metal! Goat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What I want, oh noble Lord Collector, is to be allowed to leave your realm, with safe passage and a clear path.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:55:55-08:00","id":391276,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sure. I already wrote it down, I don't like to edit my IC posts except for grammatical mistakes. So, if I made a mistake, go ahead, exploit it. I'm not playing Nate as a genius anyway, it's only fitting he gets tricked by his own words.<br /> <br /> But as a player? Sure, I see at least three ways to screw with Nate's wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:55:22-08:00","id":391360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391181#post391181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Gaius, exactly what you are asking the keeper?<br /> <br /> 1)You want to re-write the terms of the original Contract and make them retroactive.<br /> <br /> 2)You also want that anyone under the original Contracts can switch to this new one if they want.<br /> <br /> 3)Finally, as part of the new retroactive Contract you, personally not neccesarily the others, agree to explicitely become owned heart and soul by the Keeper.<br /> <br /> Are those terms correct? I want to be sure before proceeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for checking on the clarity (or Clarity...?). The first two are correct. 3) is basically right: the terms of the new retroactive Contract will include that Max becomes owned in that way by the Keeper. Provided the Keeper, er, keeps to the terms that Max lays down -- and it's in his interest that they sound reasonable to the Keeper -- that'll remain true. EDIT: As an emphasis on 1), Max did say he wants to state the terms, which isn't quite the same as negotiating with them.<br /> <br /> Though, as you said, the Keeper's just committed to hearing requests, and doesn't have to agree to the new terms once he's heard them. If he refuses, it'd probably be fair for Max to get to make a different request, but, well... Arcadia hasn't seemed big on that particular flavor of fairness. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391215#post391215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaaw, I just want to give Max a hug right now.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391223#post391223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right? He is such a sweet piece of pork <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is so. And he's crying, too, so... Sweet and salty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While I'm most nervous about what the little guy's attempting, I'm very curious to see what the Keeper does to the requests for home. C'mon, Nate and Jessica! You can wrangle a way out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Elaboration~ 02-03-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:07:01-08:00","id":391488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391276#post391276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm sure. I already wrote it down, I don't like to edit my IC posts except for grammatical mistakes. So, if I made a mistake, go ahead, exploit it. I'm not playing Nate as a genius anyway, it's only fitting he gets tricked by his own words.<br /> <br /> But as a player? Sure, I see at least three ways to screw with Nate's wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, I hope I didn't offend you, not my intention, it was only an inocent teasing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:32:56-08:00","id":391548,"title":"","content":"Thorbes, you did not offend me at all, I assure you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:36:53-08:00","id":391552,"title":"","content":"Glad to know! These things are sometimes difficult to get right, so I tend to err on the side of caution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:50:55-08:00","id":391569,"title":"","content":"It is the absence of voice and being able to see body language. It can be a real problem. Thus emote cons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:06:51-08:00","id":391594,"title":"","content":"Sorry! I'll use those next times then!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:11:14-08:00","id":391597,"title":"","content":"What a fun game this has been and I assume will continue to be!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T11:20:08-08:00","id":392755,"title":"","content":"In retrospect, I may have &quot;budded&quot; in line. I'm sorry. I guess I paniced like Jessica. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T00:37:51-08:00","id":393492,"title":"","content":"Heh, I dunno if there's really a strict line. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just so long as we all get to go in a given &quot;round,&quot; it's probably okay.<br /> <br /> 'sides, I can sympathize with feeling like your character: I'm nearly as anxious as Max about getting those terms right! ^_^o It all seemed so clear in my head when I was thinking about them, but when I actually sat down... I'm unsure they came through quite how I'd have liked. :/ Which I guess fits, given the emotional scene beforehand, but... There is the distinct possibility Max would have been better off shoving one of those apples in his mouth and looking for a plate to lie on. We'll see!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T02:54:26-08:00","id":393559,"title":"","content":"Oh, Gaius, that completely broke my heart, man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like a bastard playing the keeper now, it all felt like shits and giggles up to this point. Hope you take it as a compliment because is what it is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, could you re-write clearly the terms in this thread so I get them right. I think I know the card you are playing (very bold!) but I want to be completely sure. If it serves as consolation, I think the keeper is pridful enough as to fall completely for it. I'm a sucker for happy endings but I don't know how poor Max is goign to get away from this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:10:03-08:00","id":393720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=393559#post393559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Gaius, that completely broke my heart, man <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I feel like a bastard playing the keeper now, it all felt like shits and giggles up to this point. Hope you take it as a compliment because is what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, thanks, Thorbes. ^_^ That means a lot. That first part of the post (well, both, for different reasons) was hard for me to write; it isn't as polished as I usually like, and it made me a little uncomfortable to get it out there. I don't know if I've ever had clinical depression, but I have had issues of self-worth before and some of that seemed to sink in.<br /> <br /> If it helps, I think you're doing a great job with the Keeper. He's intimidating, and just has a lot of character shining through. You're not a bastard, you're just doing what someone has to, and doing it well. Take heart: one way or another, this should be ending soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, could you re-write clearly the terms in this thread so I get them right. I think I know the card you are playing (very bold!) but I want to be completely sure. </div> </div> </div>Certainly. And yeah, &quot;go big or go home,&quot; is definitely the phrase for it. So, in addition to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=391360#post391360\">those outlined</a>, about others with similar contracts being able to switch to the new terms, all of this being retroactive, and the terms including that Max will be owned heart and soul, here are the terms:<br /> <br /> 1) The Keeper sells the first buyer the item in question, which means as laid out:<br /> 1a) The Keeper agrees (in this formal contract) that he can no longer own it.<br /> 1b) The Keeper agrees (in this formal contract) that the buyer is given sole ownership of it.<br /> 2) The Keeper takes ownership of the buyer, explicitly including the buyer's heart, the buyer's soul, the buyer's everything.<br /> 2a) The Keeper takes ownership of these in the broadest sense, and takes not a bit less.<br /> 2b) This ownership will allow the Keeper to be within his rights for everything he's done to Max, and anything further he cares to do.<br /> <br /> If the above is true, then the Contract holds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it serves as consolation, I think the keeper is pridful enough as to fall completely for it. I'm a sucker for happy endings but I don't know how poor Max is goign to get away from this... </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'm a sucker for the same, so I'm hopeful things work out, too. That pride is <i>definitely</i> something on which this plan hinges. So, let's just hope the Keeper doesn't believe that the half-bawling piglet in there is trying to pull a fast one on him. ... Er, and also that I haven't borked up the terms, because if I have, I'm sorry, Max, I tried! ;_;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T07:20:52-08:00","id":393727,"title":"","content":"Gaius, you are great writer. I look forward to seeing what you do. On a lesser note, I was proud of Jessica for remembering her tattoo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T08:43:54-08:00","id":393782,"title":"","content":"I also feel so bad reading Max's plea. x) I agree with Cire and Thorbes, this was hard to read. In a very good way.<br /> <br /> And I really don't know what you're trying to pull. Maybe it's because there's a loophole I don't get, an english technicality, but for me, Max is just sacrificing himself. But hey, if I believe that's the case, then Nate will too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:30:47-08:00","id":394122,"title":"","content":"For once, and I think this is the important part, the Keeper will no longer (and remeber, retroactively) have the right to bring the buyers of the figurines to Arcadia. Omnipotence doesn't amount to shit out of your playground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T23:33:48-08:00","id":394546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=393727#post393727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaius, you are great writer. I look forward to seeing what you do.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=393782#post393782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel so bad reading Max's plea. x) I agree with Cire and Thorbes, this was hard to read. In a very good way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you both. ^_^ I enjoy reading all of your posts, too, especially with all this drama flying around. Let's find out how it all winds up<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a lesser note, I was proud of Jessica for remembering her tattoo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd completely forgotten about that detail, but it's a clever thing to bring up. If Max blows his high-stakes gamble, remembering it could put Jessica in a better position. Even getting something as meaningful as that restored to her would be a big thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I really don't know what you're trying to pull. Maybe it's because there's a loophole I don't get, an english technicality, but for me, Max is just sacrificing himself. But hey, if I believe that's the case, then Nate will too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can understand completely. When I thought it up and rolled it around, I was really conflicted; it'll either turn out to be as clever as I think it might be, or just monumentally stupid. XD I'm also encouraged that you haven't guessed it yet; the three of you are very bright, so if it hasn't jumped out, that gives a much better chance for the Keeper to go for it believably. And if it doesn't work out, then... Well, I'll make sure it's at least clear what Max was <i>trying</i> to do. ^_^o<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=394122#post394122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For once, and I think this is the important part, the Keeper will no longer (and remeber, retroactively) have the right to bring the buyers of the figurines to Arcadia. Omnipotence doesn't amount to shit out of your playground.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Would you believe this was not actually an angle I'd considered? XD A lot of his word choices were <i>very</i> deliberate, but that bit, not so much. It's a really good idea, though; Max may be very wise to leverage it (if he thinks of it), should the core of the plan blow up in his face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T01:52:28-08:00","id":394623,"title":"","content":"Unexpected loophole for brave Max, then! That doesn't make it any less binding or effective I'm sure you'll be glad to know? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:55:48-08:00","id":395777,"title":"","content":"Man, I felt horrible writing Nate's reaction. x) Sorry Max, your arcadian role model is just a terrible person! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T21:50:37-08:00","id":397192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=394623#post394623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unexpected loophole for brave Max, then! That doesn't make it any less binding or effective I'm sure you'll be glad to know? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! Worry not, for the dude's a pig; he's more than able to make use of whatever winds up <s>in his trough</s> on his plate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=395777#post395777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I felt horrible writing Nate's reaction. x) Sorry Max, your arcadian role model is just a terrible person! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oosh, that is a pretty brutal post there; I can see why it was hard to get out. Still, it's well-written and gets across the inner turmoil and intensity. Nicely done!<br /> <br /> I don't know that Nate's so awful;* I mean, much as most people certainly hope they'll behave admirably in an intensely stressful and traumatic situation... It can be hard to know what impact it's going to have. Particularly when part of that trauma has actively tampered with the way one thinks and reacts. Wanting desperately to do what one feels is right, but not finding the strength to do so -- and hating oneself for it, to boot -- doesn't make one a terrible person: it's a very human reaction. I mean, ultimately finding the strength is also a human reaction, but I'd be hard-pressed to call the one who can't a terrible person just because of it. I mostly just kinda feel bad for Nate.<br /> <br /> * I know the smiley means you weren't 100% serious, but I felt like a yammer and it seemed a good jumping off point. ^_^<br /> <br /> Though, as a sidebar, thinking back to Max and Nate's interactions, especially when wandering around earlier... I now imagine there's an alternate reality where the two wound up in a very different Arcadian Realm. In which they play out something like the Pleasure Island segment from Disney's Pinnochio, with Max filling in for the wooden boy and Nate for Lampwick. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> ... Hmm, also starring Jessica Cricket?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T15:21:38-08:00","id":398105,"title":"","content":"Ha! The Pleasure Island metaphor is spot on. <br /> <br /> Sure, Nate's behavior is understandable, but with this post, I was mostly pointing out one of his major flaws : his arrogance and boasting. He implied many times that he was the strongest and the smartest of the three, he berated max for not taking action when the piggie refused to pass the Fangs and Talon contract, he tried to deal with the Keeper by ensuring that either way, he'll gain power over the Zodiacs, but when it comes down to it, he's just a big selfish coward.<br /> <br /> And I looove playing it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T01:34:33-08:00","id":398595,"title":"","content":"Mmmmmm, I'm hitting a bit of a choice block here. Ok, I'll tell you what I'm planing and you tell me what do you think, ok? Max caught both the Keeper and me off guard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, The keeper originally asked what would each of you consider a proper compensation for its transgressions (not so much against you, as against the Wyrd) and it would give you a <i>chance</i> to get it.<br /> <br /> The idea was for each of you to be presented with a task or challenge appropiate to the prize and your personality.<br /> <br /> Alas! Max took an inexpected turn and offered the Keeper a deal, rather than simply asking for a compensation, and made sure that anyone could benefit from it (go big or/and go home, uh, Max?)<br /> <br /> So, Max may get a pasing in the task part as he already balanced things out with his own offering.<br /> <br /> Thing is, if Max actually get what he wants, it may render any of your tasks-prizes irrelevant (retroactivation has this things).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:51:52-08:00","id":399538,"title":"","content":"@Evilmarmelade: Oh, I'll definitely agree there. ^_^ I tend to play relatively low-key characters, but I've had a lot of fun with arrogant, bombastic sorts who aren't nearly as awesome as they think they are, too. There's a ton of fun to be had with that.<br /> <br /> @Thorbes: Yeah, I can understand how that might put you in a tricky position. ^_^o Part of me is wondering if I should have maybe PMed you with Max's plan. It might have made it easier to work it in (or not), while still leaving room for the tasks. And yeah, the personally-suited tasks sound like really fun and interesting set pieces; I'd hate to lose them.<br /> <br /> Still, here's a thought. Whether the characters fail or succeed at overcoming those tasks (and thus parts of themselves, to some degree)* may well have deep effects on the characters after/if they leave. So even if the tasks' prizes don't wind up counting for any of them, they could still have a definite impact. As for Max, perhaps their Keeper could prepare tasks for all three of them, noting that Max doesn't have to participate, but that it <i>would</i> please him. While also noting that he'd prefer to accept Max's terms after the fun and games, and that doesn't strictly <i>have</i> to do so. The implication would be that the Keeper may find it suspicious if Max is willing to sign away his heart and soul to make the Keeper happy, but is unwilling to amuse him like this. It may impact any decision to accept, or decide he smells a rat (no offense to the Rat).<br /> <br /> * The events themselves may also be kind of traumatic or otherwise deeply affecting.<br /> <br /> So, in that case, all three would (probably) wind up facing the interesting and/or horrible scenarios the Collector's concocted, and they could still leave a mark on their psyches. It's also possible, should Max's plan pay off and the retroactive nature of the new terms come into play, that Jessica and Nate might be entitled to arrange for different compensation if they succeeded.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T18:12:03-08:00","id":399651,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I don't really have an opinion on the question. I like the idea of having tailored trials to overcome, and I trust that you'll manage to surprise us!<br /> <br /> Do you already have your ideas planned for us three? Or at least, jessica and Nate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T02:08:46-08:00","id":400118,"title":"","content":"The idea was to confront you against one member of the Western Zodiac, but I may end up going for something more psychoactive. It would be a pity not to use all that background your characters have (tough Nate already confronted, if failed, his own demons in the shape of that fake dumped girlfriend).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-10-2015, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T11:34:59-08:00","id":400582,"title":"","content":"I like the idea. But Valerie and the future kid could also used in many other ways. On the other hand, there's still a dozen of Zodiac, Western and Eastern, that haven't been introduced, plenty of potentials there. And Nate did have this weird obsession to meet Aries, to meet someone &quot;like&quot; him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:26:08-08:00","id":400790,"title":"","content":"Also be odd for Jessica to run into Leo again lol<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:15:05-08:00","id":400838,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Aries was my bet for Nate.<br /> <br /> As for Jessica, yes, I was thinking him or Tauro wich has an eye less and an axe to grind.<br /> <br /> Max may encounter Libra again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:33:27-08:00","id":401088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=400838#post400838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Aries was my bet for Nate.<br /> <br /> As for Jessica, yes, I was thinking him or Tauro wich has an eye less and an axe to grind.<br /> <br /> Max may encounter Libra again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aries and Libra would indeed not surprise me for Nate and Max, though I think I completely missed that the bull Derek saved Jessica from was Taurus. XD<br /> <br /> Those three would indeed work pretty solidly, for clear reasons (similarities in all three cases (goats, bovines, and ones doing the law's work or trying to set the law). Alternatives could include:<ul><li><u>Leo</u> - Could work for Nate (settling a mutual disdain, and maybe a &quot;here's what a <i>real</i> leader's like&quot; jab, even if Leo's actually kind of a cowardly bully himself) or Jessica (there's some emotional distress, especially since she feels she betrayed her boyfriend for the Contract). Max could work, but more in an &quot;animal kingdom's mismatch of the century&quot; kinda way.</li> <li><u>Sagittarius</u> - Could be a pretty natural fit for Max, the Keeper feeling that the one who helped Max should balance the scales by hindering him. He never met Nate or Jessica, so the connections aren't great. Given Sagi's (apparent) heroics, I could see that rubbing Nate the wrong way. Not sure how he and Jessica would interact.</li> <li><u>Pisces</u> - Nate had a certain interest in his powers, but... Yeah, honestly, there's not a strong case here. Nah.</li> <li><u>Monkey</u> - What a tweest! It turns out Derek functionally gave up more than he meant to in surrendering his last name, or -- by way of another deal -- maybe has a chance of getting it back. Or whatever. Jessica would make the most interesting match-up, while Nate could... Yeah, see Sagittarius, basically. He and Max never interacted and don't have a ton in common. I guess similar to Libra, they've got a connection via law/contracts: Derek cut one he might now regret, while Max is cutting one he's not sure about.</li> <li><u>Surprise!</u> - Whether another member of the Western or Eastern Zodiacs yet unmentioned, another of the Keeper's Changelings from elsewhere (perhaps an older collection), the Secretary (he knew an impressive Contract to teach to Derek), the Keeper himself, their own Fetches, alternate reality/future takes on the characters, images of loved ones from their true lives, and on and on and on. The sky's the limit here!</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Shockingly, Aquarius is not Pisces. Also, Sagittarius misspelled. 02-11-2015, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T01:36:47-08:00","id":401630,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions, Gaius! Very well thought too. It never had crossed my mind to use Derek that way (guy kinda fell in the background) but is an interesting way to introduce him back in. He may also volunteer to actually help any of you as he himself may be already Lost.<br /> <br /> As for Taurus, yeah, I don't think Nyrufa wanted him to be so, but seemed easy enough to make that jump of logic. As he had a very tense moment with Jessica it would be a pity not to use him at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T02:53:51-08:00","id":401693,"title":"","content":"I think you mixed Aquarius with Pisces. And yeah, they wouldn't be my first choice for Nate anyway.<br /> <br /> And I agree, great ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T06:38:09-08:00","id":401810,"title":"","content":"So, Thorbes, should we wait until you've posted our trials, or do you want us to answer to our disappearance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T09:57:37-08:00","id":401986,"title":"","content":"Danke. ^_^ Just took all the players that have been encountered and checked through the lot of them. Followed by random brainstorming in the &quot;other&quot; bucket. Given the framing of the trial, we may even wind up dealing with more than one &quot;adversary&quot; apiece.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=401630#post401630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It never had crossed my mind to use Derek that way (guy kinda fell in the background) but is an interesting way to introduce him back in. He may also volunteer to actually help any of you as he himself may be already Lost.<br /> <br /> As for Taurus, yeah, I don't think Nyrufa wanted him to be so, but seemed easy enough to make that jump of logic. As he had a very tense moment with Jessica it would be a pity not to use him at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did think it'd be nice to get all four of our original characters involved in the game's last/penultimate act (for now). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Whatever winds up happening with Derek, that kind of symmetry would be nice.<br /> <br /> And there we go, that makes sense on Taurus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=401693#post401693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you mixed Aquarius with Pisces. And yeah, they wouldn't be my first choice for Nate anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh, so it is! XD I'm amused that Nyrufa and I both screwed that up, and in different ways. I've edited in the change.<br /> <br /> I have also just recalled with amusement that Aries is a ram and Capricorn is a (sea-)goat. This amuses me, as &quot;doubling-up&quot; on any sort of animal within the western zodiac stands out given the crazy diversity in the other ten signs.<br /> <br /> And yeah, pending further instruction, I shall presume Thorbes will write up the arrival sites before we get to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:51:52-08:00","id":402519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=401810#post401810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Thorbes, should we wait until you've posted our trials, or do you want us to answer to our disappearance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll make a follow up post detailing where each of you appear, unless you want to take care of that yourselves:<br /> <br /> -Basically you all appear at different entrances of a garden-labyrinth/maze* that extends as far as the eye can see. You have to cross it.<br /> <br /> *We only have one word for this in my language and always get confused with these two terms. Which were the differences again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:18:29-08:00","id":402533,"title":"","content":"Sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=402519#post402519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*We only have one word for this in my language and always get confused with these two terms. Which were the differences again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They can be used synonymously here, so you'd be fine either way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So far as connotations go, &quot;labyrinth&quot; is probably what you'd prefer, as it tends to imply an especially difficult or dangerous maze and carries more mythic connotations; it comes from the Greek myth of Theseus and the minotaur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:52:33-08:00","id":402577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=402519#post402519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll make a follow up post detailing where each of you appear, unless you want to take care of that yourselves:<br /> <br /> -Basically you all appear at different entrances of a garden-labyrinth/maze* that extends as far as the eye can see. You have to cross it.<br /> <br /> *We only have one word for this in my language and always get confused with these two terms. Which were the differences again? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I won't be able to write a detailed post until tomorrow, afternoon, which is precisely around the times you usually write your posts, Thorbes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (No, I'm not stalking you, that's silly. You're silly.) So, no post for me I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T15:26:34-08:00","id":407064,"title":"","content":"Triple-post is up!<br /> <br /> Ok, here is the deal, imagine the garden as big circle and the signs entrances disposed around like the hours on a clock, each of you enters through one of these doors and must mange to exit trough the opossite, so if you entered through 12 o'clock you must exist through 6. That means each of you will face two of the Western Zodiacs, one at the entrance and another one before you can claim your prize.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-15-2015, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:03:04-08:00","id":407246,"title":"","content":"Huh. Which means, if we follow the Western Zodiac's order, that Max and Nate are on opposite entrances, and that both of them will face Aries and Libra, albeit in a different order. (And jessica would face Scorpio)<br /> <br /> Unless you use a completely different order, Thorbes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:45:44-08:00","id":407338,"title":"","content":"Ooh, interesting setup, Thorbes. ^_^ Two adversaries each at either end, with a chance for the characters to run into one another and help or hinder each other (Nate and Max in particular, if Evilmarmelade is correct). Never mind that there are likely to be more adversaries and challenges throughout the maze, to say nothing of the maze itself. This looks like a really great set piece, rich with potential.<br /> <br /> ... Also, it occurs to me the Keeper could probably snare a large number of mortals if he marketed this kinda thing as a reality TV show with heavy game show components.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of 