North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T02:27:03-07:00","id":558035,"title":"","content":"It is an understandable and based concern. After all if you don't uphold your part of the bargain, the Keeper is under no obligation to uphold its. That said, how much can you stretch the wording of the rerquirement to &quot;cross the maze&quot; and still count, that you don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T08:47:50-07:00","id":559416,"title":"","content":"Aye. Max is also worried that the Wilds won't play nice, but this is his main concern. The kid's struggling with himself between making a break for it with his friends, and giving them a way out while he tries to muddle through to the end. An end he still isn't sure how to find, granted. In any case, for a pig coated in mud, he's not having a good time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:49:20-07:00","id":563459,"title":"","content":"Okay, answered. Sorry, I've been distracted for weeks with many things. It's not going better, since I need to find a job, but I'm not giving up on this game, especially since it will soon be one year old!<br /> <br /> And yes, my answer is short, but I don't know what else Nate could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T04:00:53-07:00","id":563942,"title":"","content":"Ow! Well, good luck with the job hunting! I don't know if things are as harsh there in the land of the Franks as they are here in Spain, but in any case keep your hopes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T15:16:13-07:00","id":564648,"title":"","content":"Wow. Sorry to hear that, Evilmarmelade. &gt;_&lt; I remember being out of work for about a year, and have all the sympathy in the world for anyone conducting a job search. Best of luck on getting through! If you could use some venting or other moral support, you know where to find it.<br /> <br /> And it's a good post you've made. I sometimes think I belabor mine too much because they don't feel as long as they &quot;should,&quot; but that's seldom needed: 'brevity is the soul of wit,' and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-22-2015, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:47:02-07:00","id":568704,"title":"","content":"I too am sorry to hear about all the challenges faced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T21:39:11-07:00","id":568756,"title":"","content":"So to recap the Seemings<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast - Go feral<br /> <br /> <br /> Darkling - Stab someone's back<br /> <br /> <br /> Fairest - Lead a revolt<br /> <br /> <br /> Ogre - Mentally snap<br /> <br /> <br /> Elemental - At one with your environment<br /> <br /> <br /> Wizened - Unrevealed.<br /> <br /> <br /> These are the methods of escape for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T23:48:23-07:00","id":568882,"title":"","content":"Does that mean.... Max is on his way to become a Fairest?<br /> <br /> Now THAT'S a plot twist!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:42:42-07:00","id":571717,"title":"","content":"I think the 2e Seemings are a little broader than that. But yeah, should things work out and Max get a Seeming, that seems a likely one. Definitely an odd combo, alright. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, I had thinking Thorbes might want to handle the results of the magic -- I'll take the rap for neither making that clear nor, y'know, asking about it to confirm -- but figured I'd mosey things along. ^_^o If you'd prefer it take a different shape, Thorbes, just say the word!<br /> <br /> In other news, forecasts could call for some tension between the cloven-hooved dudes, and Jessica is meeting what may or may not be the Cheshire Cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:56:05-07:00","id":572486,"title":"","content":"Working on it!<br /> <br /> Well, that means Jessica is an Ogre, Max indeed looks like a Fairest (though we don't know yet how the Wizened work) and Nate is as Darkling as it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:26:16-07:00","id":573269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=572486#post572486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nate is as Darkling as it gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he? Nate didn't actually stab anyone in the back. He thought he would be ready to, he thought himself superior to the others, but he's gradually relying on others for help and support.<br /> He went feral in his fight against Max and his climb of the mountain, he tried to lead a revolt with the tribunal by tricking the Keeper...<br /> <br /> Really, the thing that most define Nate for now is failure : almost everything he attempted to do backfired. The only thing he got from this is his Vainglory Contract. I think Nate didn't get his... defining moment yet, contrary to Jessica who decided to snap and smash through everything, or Max who relies on his contracts and plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:34:11-07:00","id":573281,"title":"","content":"Maybe he's an Elemental, gradually letting go of his ego and becoming part of the collective, as opposed to an individual? He did seem pretty egotistical when he first came in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T15:49:53-07:00","id":573297,"title":"","content":"Seem? He WAS super egotistical. x)<br /> <br /> He's losing his ego, sure, but he doesn't have any 'collective' to hold on for now,except his two companions, and it's not really elemental material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:11:25-07:00","id":573376,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Nate's trickier to peg. Of the three, he certainly had the clearest <i>trajectory</i> toward Darkling, but didn't really go through with the necessary betrayal, nor make some other sort of hard &quot;I did what had to be done,&quot; decision. If I had to pick one for him right now, it probably would be Elemental, as he seems closest to the Elemental 'arc'* of going from super-egotistical to much more humble, but I'd feel iffy about it. I think Evilmarmelade is right on the money: Nate's defining moment is yet to come.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to finding out what it is. ^_^<br /> <br /> * Just copying this from a blog comment, since Dave noted these were good summaries and they go into more detail than one line easily could:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;<br /> Beasts were imprisoned or hedged in by societal norms, took the offer of somebody liberating them, which landed them in even more trouble. They learned that they had to rescue themselves and set their own rules, but they will never stand to be restrained again.<br /> <br /> Darklings were loyal to a fault, until they were betrayed, and fell pray to somebody who offered trust. They learned to put their own needs before those of others, but they can never trust again.<br /> <br /> Fairests were fonts of untapped potential restrained by laziness, despair, or timidity. They accepted a chance to shine, which turned out to be more of the same. They Escaped by standing up for themselves and showing their skill, their inner talent, but they are still reluctant to thrust themselves into the spotlight.<br /> <br /> Ogres were victims of abuse. They took it and took it unti they snapped and tried to get away. They Escaped when they realized that they couldn\u2019t run, they had to turn around and fight; hit others before they hit you. However, they can\u2019t stand to be reminded of their inner weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Elementals were people undone by their vanity and ego. They learned to humble themselves, see themselves as part of the big picture. They now act without a thought for themselves, but they are badly affected when their actions damage the larger world.<br /> &quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:18:57-07:00","id":573380,"title":"","content":"If we go by his past only, then Elemental could work sure, but so could Fairest : after all, he managed to get through life by lazying around, only picking up some skills as a musician because it was fun. If he had decided to focus seriously on his music, he could have done some great stuff, but instead he prefered to party. And the spotlight thing could work, with his guilt gnawing at him.<br /> <br /> And Elemental... well, we have the first part. Now, let's just see how the rest of his adventures will happen : who knows, maybe he will finally become the fabled Metal Goat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:49:16-07:00","id":573436,"title":"","content":"Would be nice for the element to come into things for at least one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still time for someone to snag an Elements Contract, though!<br /> <br /> Very good point on the Fairest angle. Hadn't really been looking at Nate that way -- it's a significant part of him, much as the ego is rather prominent -- but he'd fit well there, too. ^_^<br /> <br /> Though I think Jessica indicates that there's such a thing as overemphasizing the backstory side of the Seeming writeups. I think she'd work well as an Ogre, but I also didn't get the sense she was abused before she was taken. Likewise, it's easy to imagine someone who didn't start incredibly loyal then becoming a Darkling by making a decision to betray someone or some other sort of &quot;hard but necessary choice.&quot; I feel Max fits the Fairest backstory surprisingly well, but it's neither exclusive to him nor necessary.*<br /> <br /> * In turning down the Boar, I do get the sense he's probably passed pretty decisively on Beast or Ogre.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think you're right that it's gonna depend on how things play out. Nate might wind up with any of them, or Jessica or Max might find reason to head toward a different path. Still plenty of game in screwed-up fairytale land to go!<br /> <br /> Or maybe Wizened'll come out and all of us will say, &quot;Ohh, yeah, you can't get Nate-ier than that.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T03:25:59-07:00","id":573705,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm quite curious on what the shtick of Wizened would be, specially after seeing the description of Wizened Kiths. They were all some sort of bio-mechanical stuff, or parts of you substituted by tools and such. No idea really.<br /> <br /> ON second thought, I have to agree with you guys, Nate was definitely on the way of becoming a Darkling a lot of times but never actually went trough with it. Fairest does fit better, but is probably too soon to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:09:15-07:00","id":574015,"title":"","content":"Well from what I've been able to gather, the 2nd Edition Seemings are practically a 180 from the first edition versions.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st edition Beasts were about forsaking their primal urges, 2nd edition is about embracing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st edition Darklings were about coming out of the darkness, 2nd edition is about plunging yourself into it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st edition Ogres were about overcoming barbarism and gaining a moment of intelligence, 2nd edition is about snapping after so long of abuse and slaughtering everything in your path.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st edition Elementals were about regaining one's sense of individuality and separating yourself from nature, 2nd edition is about giving up your sense of individuality and bonding with nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1st edition Fairest were about being chosen because of your exceptional talent and skill, 2nd edition is about you finding the talent and skill you never knew you had.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if the pattern holds, we can expect some manner of switch-around for Wizened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:33:40-07:00","id":574672,"title":"","content":"Wizened is up! Annnnnnd I don't expect all of us will say, &quot;Ohh, yeah, you can't get Nate-ier than that.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I <i>think</i> the pattern can still hold, depending on one's viewpoint. 1st edition Wizened were spoken of as being diminished by their Durances, while 2nd edition Wizened strip away parts of themselves they find unnecessary or inferior. Still... kinda rolling that one around, I guess. I don't know that I find it as punchy or interesting as the other 5, at least by its current presentation or my current read.<br /> <br /> <i>All</i> of them can be said to be about casting out something personal that's had held them back -- be it civility, trust, passivity, feeling, or ego. Wizened seem to be more about casting out nearly everything obstructing their craft (so they can get free of the biggest obstruction to their order, Arcadia). It's... distinct, I guess, but I dunno how I feel about it. I'm not really feeling them yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T05:26:15-07:00","id":575069,"title":"","content":"Sooooo, the 2nd Edition Wizened is Stanley Gimble?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videoc