like this comes first. The heads up you've given us is very much appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:47:31-07:00","id":656820,"title":"","content":"That's awesome, Evilmarmalade! Kudos to you, friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:35:10-07:00","id":657030,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear things are getting better for you, man! Hope you don't have too much trouble settling yourself into a new place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T07:22:12-07:00","id":661864,"title":"","content":"Thanks you guys!<br /> <br /> Thorbes, are you sure you don't want our help to continue the story? Tell us what's the problem, which part you're having trouble with, and we will give you suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T09:49:48-07:00","id":662020,"title":"","content":"Sorry.<br /> <br /> Ok, here's the thing, I sort of know how I want those ruins to look like and one of the things I want there,but I need more.<br /> <br /> In general lines:<br /> <br /> Circular stone structure with several arcs.<br /> <br /> Arcs look like old metal mirrors<br /> <br /> mirrors show things past present and future<br /> <br /> mirrors are also portals<br /> <br /> I know what does appear in some of those mirrors but I need more things","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:12:54-07:00","id":663093,"title":"","content":"Let's see. Some arcs could be broken, symbolizing the death of some zodiac people (we already know about Taurus, maybe some other Western Zodiac already bit the dust?).<br /> <br /> I think the ruins should have inhabitants : maybe hedge beasts, or hobgoblins, either guarding this location or just defending their nest.<br /> <br /> A central fountain that soothes pain and heal injuries, but causes drinkers to forget a few memories each time they take a mouthful, eventually closing down some mirrors or portals due to the drinker's past not existing anymore.<br /> <br /> Tapestries retelling the legends of the two Zodiacs.<br /> <br /> The Horse! He's stuck in there, trapped in a mirror or confused by illusions from them!<br /> <br /> As with Max, maybe a chance for Nate and Jessica to exactly choose which animal to embody and how. For Jess, the peaceful cow or maybe one of its cousins : a bison, an auroch... For Nate, a sheep, who prefers safety in numbers and has a lot of companions, a fierce ram who protects his flock, or maybe a lonely mouflon, who just decides to do whatever the hell he wants alone.<br /> <br /> I'll try to come up with additional ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T12:30:17-07:00","id":663386,"title":"","content":"No worries, Thorbes. There are a lot of directions this could go. Sometimes just getting thoughts out of your head, talking them through with people, and maybe getting a little outside input can help things fall into place. ^_^<br /> <br /> You've got a good setup, and Evilmarmelade's led off with some great suggestions! Think I'll babble a bit with some notions...<br /> <br /> - <u>Memories Rewoven:</u><br /> Portals to the past, at least some of them, lead into memories of particular people -- perhaps just those present, perhaps even more. Past events play out as they did before, and visitors are (mostly) ignored. However, should they change the course of events in some way, this has an effect on whomever held that memory. How this works, well... Options are plentiful:<br /> + The past actually changes and ripples forward, at least in some limited fashion.<br /> + The person remembers the new events instead of the old. May make no sense if they stop to think about it, or other memories may change to accommodate it.<br /> + Memories shift their emotional tenor. E.g. Someone depresses or cheers up memory!person, so memory!person feels worse or better about that memory, perhaps with personal/developmental impacts.<br /> + People/Things can be taken out of the memory by visitors and back into the Hedge.<br /> ... To some extent, I guess the above can actually work quite well for present and future portals. Neat possibilities there, too.<br /> <br /> - <u>Thoughts for Visions:</u><br /> + What the trio's (and/or maybe even other Zodiac members') loved ones have been up to back on Earth -- or those who may be important if/when they return.<br /> + Messages of advice/sorrow/comfort/rage/hope/whatevs from their future selves -- or, oddly, from their past selves, perhaps about things they've forgotten.<br /> + Depictions of what brought the Western and Eastern Zodiac members to be as they are -- ditto the Scribe and Collector, for that matter.<br /> + Details about Summernickel and Winterdime -- or perhaps those they've helped (or even hurt) in the past.<br /> <br /> - <u>The Guide:</u><br /> A strange individual -- trusted by one of the goblins and distrusted by the other -- offers to show Jessica and Nate some important portals/images/paths. These <i>will</i> leave an impact, but...<br /> + Are they for the better? For the worse? Or is that up to the two of them?<br /> + Does the guide have some beneficent or malicious intent, or is this simply what the guide does with visitors?<br /> + What opinions does this guide foster -- and what actions might the guide take -- should there be any damages, tampering, or other impacts to the arcs or portals?<br /> + What relation, if any, does this guide have to the Collector?<br /> <br /> - <u>Zodiac Pursuit:</u><br /> It may be further from their domain than the Collector would want them to be (though oaths could have things covered), but perhaps one or more members of Eastern or Western Zodiac could pursue or put in an appearance. If you thought up any scenarios you were really hoping to use, this could be a good window. It wouldn't really need to be them, either, given the weirdly out-of-space and -time nature of the place.<br /> <br /> - <u>The Collector:</u><br /> Oh shit! The Keeper's not about to let Summernickel or Winterdime carry out a repeat performance with his charges, and comes in person!<br /> + Still, outside the heart of his realm, his powers are merely very powerful instead of outright godlike.<br /> +Perhaps even something about that particular place leaves him especially vulnerable -- perhaps the goblins choose that location for this reason.<br /> + Should Max stagger through to the end, the Keeper may be forced back early to address that bit of business, or at least divide his attention/power.<br /> +The Keeper may aim to simply keep the Goat and Ox preoccupied.<br /> + Or this may come paired with the above &quot;Zodiac Pursuit,&quot; whether to support the Keeper (while he's less imposing than usual), or for the Keeper to support his loyal -- or at least not actively escaping -- Zodiac members with magic or mind games (possibly because direct action is forbidden to him there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Modified formatting. 09-13-2015, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:12:06-07:00","id":666024,"title":"","content":"New ideas!<br /> <br /> <u>Guess what! Winterdime/Summernickel aren't who they look like!</u><br /> -He's a pawn of the Keeper, or even one of his servitors shapeshifted as an answer to Summernickel's appearance. And he's ready to backstab the trio as soon as they reach the ruin!<br /> -He's actually working for another Gentry, who would be <i>delighted</i> at the idea of stealing not one, but two of the most prized possesions of his old rival, the Magnificent Collector.<br /> -Plot Twist ahoy! He was sent by none other than the Secretary, who has secretely decided to rig the game in his favor. But who is he, and what's his goal?<br /> <br /> <u>Poison! Poisonous poison!</u><br /> Hey, remember when Winterdime offered the duo a strange fruit and Nate ate all of it, including the leaves? Good times! Yeah, turns out this wasn't a good idea. But what are its effects? Narcoleptic? Petrification? Temporarily robs the Goat of one of his senses? Shifts the bone structure to force him to go on all four? Get him happy but high?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T02:17:59-07:00","id":666631,"title":"","content":"Evilmarmelade is evil. He figured out some of the twists. Damm! That's what I get for playing with smart, imaginative and intelligent people; when will I learn?<br /> <br /> EDIT: small post to set the scene for Nate and Jessica, second round of combat for Mighty Max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-16-2015, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T11:41:05-07:00","id":667307,"title":"","content":"I fear I have lost computer access for the moment. (I am at my parents currently.) I will try to fix this ASAP. Also good scene Thorbes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  added text 09-16-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T16:21:31-07:00","id":667556,"title":"","content":"By the way, I noticed the fist page was outdated. I never even listed Evilmarmelade as one of the players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've gone back and fixed that.<br /> <br /> This one is playing out nicely. Might be interested in rerunning it under second edition themes in the future, where we aren't necessarily forced to have an all Beast cast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:15:19-07:00","id":667623,"title":"","content":"Good scene is indeed good. ^_^ Those were some fine suggestions, Evilmarmelade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=666631#post666631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mighty Max</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why it didn't occur to me sooner, but now <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7VSBkq0n1Ks\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is in my head. It would have been a... slightly different spin on things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=667307#post667307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear I have lost computer access for the moment. (I am at my parents currently.) I will try to fix this ASAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ack, sorry to hear about losing your computer access, Cire. :/ For your own sake more than the game,* here's hoping you get back a machine of your own soon.<br /> <br /> * Though definitely also for the game. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=667556#post667556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I noticed the fist page was outdated. I never even listed Evilmarmelade as one of the players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've gone back and fixed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for updating that, Nyrufa. =)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This one is playing out nicely. Might be interested in rerunning it under second edition themes in the future, where we aren't necessarily forced to have an all Beast cast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>You're right that things might play out a bit differently; anyone keen on a particular Seeming (or able to recognize some suggestions thereof as things naturally develop) might have an easier time setting things up. That could make a difference in how things are set up, post-escape. Likewise, knowing all of the Kiths ahead of time might have also tweaked some developmental choices.<br /> <br /> That said, we've been playing out the Durance itself, and mostly loose with the rules and concepts at that. I don't know how different the core of it would be. Regardless of edition, the premise is that all PCs are their respective zodiac animals, even if the exact Kith might be in flux (just as it was here). Even in this game, Seeming hasn't yet manifested itself even at this late stage. Though from the sound of speculation here, I'm getting the sense that the Goat, Ox, and Pig might well wind up with 2e Seemings in the end in any case. We shall see!<br /> <br /> Which is all completely beside the point: It would indeed be cool to see this run again sometime. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:22:31-07:00","id":667629,"title":"","content":"Well I like free forms like this because they're much easier to run and promote better writing experience than keeping piles of dice to determine outcomes. That does mean there are times when players get carried away and pull the invincibility card, but when that happens, I tend to crack down if it gets out of hand. There have only been a few cases where I got fed up with repeat offenders and just used my GM powers to kill them off in order to get the message across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-16-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T17:38:42-07:00","id":667640,"title":"","content":"Oh, make no mistake: I definitely enjoy gaming near the free form end of the spectrum. I think that helped this game be as fun and interesting as it wound up being.* There are difficulties, as you note, but if everyone's on the same page about things -- and I get the sense that most C:tL players sitting down to play out a Durance are tacitly agreeing that their characters will see no small amount of hardship -- it tends to work very, very nicely.<br /> <br /> * And quicker and smoother! I do enjoy dice in some contexts, but I've observed they can sometimes bog things down a bit or inject an unnatural break in the action. In PbP, where things already default to slower than most would prefer, every little bit can make a big difference. Aside from all that: the game's in Arcadia! It's appropriate that things depend less on die-borne random determination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T01:11:11-07:00","id":667985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=666631#post666631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evilmarmelade is evil. He figured out some of the twists. Damm! That's what I get for playing with smart, imaginative and intelligent people; when will I learn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oneiromancy, dude!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc?p=667556#post667556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I noticed the fist page was outdated. I never even listed Evilmarmelade as one of the players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've gone back and fixed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, I'm legit! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Side note: I won't be able to post until Sunday, or maybe late Saturday. Quite the busy week I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:30:41-07:00","id":671992,"title":"","content":"Double post : Sorry, I have a cold and I didn't have much time to think of a more productive post, I didn't really feel like inventing something, since I'm not exactly sure what are these mirrors showing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","ran